Japan's prime minister went on X asking regular people to check their servers, and a company that vouches for websites being safe
turned out to be guarding its master keys with the number four.

16
00:01:36,334 --> 00:01:45,604
人们称这是最黑暗的十月，而 AI 处于这一切的核心，
它在寻找漏洞、利用漏洞，有时甚至能自动搞破坏。
People are calling it the darkest October, and AI is in the middle of almost all of
it, finding the holes, exploiting them, and sometimes wrecking things all by itself.

17
00:01:46,062 --> 00:01:51,652
每个应用都建立在多层软件堆栈上，而本周几乎每一层都出现了裂缝。
So every app sits on a stack of software layers, and this week nearly every layer cracked.

18
00:01:52,238 --> 00:01:57,316
最底层是 Linux，它运行着世界上大部分的服务器，基本上就是整个云端的基础。
At the bottom is Linux, running most of the world's servers and basically the whole cloud.

19
00:01:57,742 --> 00:02:03,812
云服务公司将一台大机器分割成隔离的虚拟机，租给不同的客户使用。
Cloud companies split one big machine into sealed-off virtual machines rented to different customers.

20
00:02:04,462 --> 00:02:13,444
10 月 15 日，一个漏洞公开，允许有人从其中一个虚拟机中逃逸并获取根权限，
这意味着获得宿主机及其上所有人的完整管理权。
On October 15th, a bug went public that let someone inside one of those break out and grab root,
meaning full admin control over the host and everyone on it.

21
00:02:13,966 --> 00:02:21,520
来自 Pwn.ai 的自动化 AI 安全引擎发现了它，而 Linus Torvalds 在前一天就合并了修复补丁。
An autonomous AI security engine from Pwn.ai found it, and Linus Torvalds merged the fix a day earlier.

22
00:02:21,774 --> 00:02:27,920
还有另一个让普通用户获得管理权限的 Linux 漏洞，以及一个 TIDB 数据库缺陷。
At another Linux bug handing regular users admin rights, plus a TIDB database flaw.

23
00:02:28,110 --> 00:02:33,028
再往上一层是 Nginx，它是数百万个网站前门的守门软件。
One layer up is Nginx, the software standing at the front door of millions of websites.

24
00:02:33,230 --> 00:02:38,372
10 月 14 日，它修复了五个漏洞，其中三个的评分高达 9.2 分。
On October 14th, it patched five bugs, three rated 9.2 out of 10.

25
00:02:38,958 --> 00:02:48,640
有些漏洞允许构造请求导致内存溢出并运行攻击者的代码或让网站崩溃，
还有一个漏洞破坏了双向身份验证，导致攻击者可以直接闯入。
Some let a crafted request overflow memory and run the attacker's code or crash the site,
and one breaks the check where both sides show ID badges, so attackers walk right past it.

26
00:02:48,814 --> 00:02:55,012
