In 1859, Bernhard Riemann found that the way primes are scattered is controlled by a set of special points,
and he guessed they all sit on one perfectly straight line.

152
00:17:21,934 --> 00:17:24,708
数百个定理都是建立在他正确的假设之上的。
Hundreds of theorems are built on the assumption he was right.

153
00:17:25,102 --> 00:17:31,012
然而在 160 多年里，没有人能证明这些点不会偏离那条线太远。
Yet for over 160 years, nobody could even prove those points don't stray far from that line.

154
00:17:31,534 --> 00:17:42,240
OpenAI 的模型声称建立了一道围栏，证明它们无法存在于可能隐藏整类相关函数的区域外，
同时排除了困扰数学家数十年的西格尔零点这种异常点。
OpenAI's model claims to have built a fence, proving none of them can exist in the outer part of the zone where they could hide for a
whole family of related functions, while also ruling out a rogue point

155
00:17:42,240 --> 00:17:45,924
OpenAI 的模型声称建立了一道围栏，证明它们无法存在于可能隐藏整类相关函数的区域外，
同时排除了困扰数学家数十年的西格尔零点这种异常点。
called the Siegel Zero that's haunted mathematicians for decades.

156
