He grew up in an elite Hungarian math class, doing eight hours of math a week, got his PhD in Bonn, and spent over a decade at Google,
where he was the lead author behind Inception.

212
00:25:16,686 --> 00:25:28,324
那是一个经典的图像识别网络，相关的论文展示了 AI 如何被微小的图像调整所欺骗，
并共同创建了几乎出现在每本 AI 教科书中的批归一化。
a classic image recognition network, and the paper showing AI can be fooled by tiny
image tweaks and co-created batch normalization, which is in basically every AI textbook.

213
00:25:28,718 --> 00:25:32,772
2023 年，他成为了 XAI 的 12 位创始人之一。
In 2023, he became one of XAI's 12 founders.

214
00:25:33,390 --> 00:25:42,884
2019 年，他预测到 2029 年 AI 将通过学习将人类数学
转化为计算机可核查的证明，从而成为超凡的数学家。
In 2019, he predicted AI would become a superhuman mathematician by
2029 by learning to turn human math into computer-checkable proofs.

215
00:25:43,502 --> 00:25:45,920
到了 2024 年，他把这个时间提前了三年。
In 2024, he moved that up three years.

216
00:25:46,254 --> 00:25:53,476
Gary Marcus 提出了反对意见，而 Segedi、Betkeras 的创造者
Francois Chollet 等人认为这将在 2026 年 6 月之前发生。
Gary Marcus pushed back, and Segedi Betkeras creator Francois Chollet and others it would happen before June 2026.

217
00:25:53,966 --> 00:25:58,948
随后在今年 5 月，OpenAI 证明了一个有 80 年历史的几何猜想。
Then this year, OpenAI disproved an 80-year-old geometry conjecture in May.

218
00:25:59,214 --> 00:26:11,110
Anthropic 研究人员在 7 月份利用 Claude Mythos 5 推翻了一个 1939 年的猜想；
而在 9 月 4 日，Anthropic 的内部模型仅用 11 天就写出了
Anthropic researchers used Claude Fable 5 to knock down a conjecture from 1939 in July, and on September 4th,
Anthropic's internal model wrote a computer-checked proof of Fermat's last theorem, which took humans over 350 years in just 11 days.

219
00:26:11,110 --> 00:26:16,740
费马大定理的计算机核查证明，而人类此前耗时超过 350 年。
Anthropic researchers used Claude Fable 5 to knock down a conjecture from 1939 in July, and on September 4th,
Anthropic's internal model wrote a computer-checked proof of Fermat's last theorem, which took humans over 350 years in just 11 days.

220
00:26:17,326 --> 00:26:19,748
他的文章从他高中毕业那天开始。
His essay starts at his high school graduation.

221
00:26:20,334 --> 00:26:23,492
最后一场考试后的两个小时是他一生中最自由的时刻。
The two hours after his final exam were the freest of his life.

222
00:26:23,886 --> 00:26:30,756
随后是空虚感，没有比赛，也没有人教导他，而且
他第一次发现如果没有这些，他不知道自己是谁。
Then came emptiness, with no competitions and nobody teaching him, and for the first time he didn't know who he was without it.

223
00:26:31,214 --> 00:26:33,760
他说这就是数学家即将感受到的东西。
He says that's what mathematicians are about to feel.

224
00:26:33,966 --> 00:26:43,620
对他来说，纯数学是一片没有地图的丛林，甚至比巴拿马和哥伦比亚之间的达里恩缺口还要糟糕，
新手在那里会迷路、感染疟疾或被吃掉。
To him, pure math is a jungle with no map, worse than the Darien Gap between
Panama and Colombia, where beginners get lost, catch malaria, or get eaten.

225
00:26:44,174 --> 00:26:47,940
探险家们绘制地图，寻找宝藏，并发明工具。
Explorers draw maps, find treasure, and invent tools.

226
00:26:48,558 --> 00:26:58,660
英雄们攀登无人涉足的高山，而且大多数人并不在乎普通人能用的宝藏，
比如最终用于在线加密的椭圆曲线，除非他们正在写申请经费。
The heroes climb mountains nobody has climbed, and most don't care about treasure regular people could use,
like elliptic curves ending up in online encryption, unless they're writing funding applications.

227
00:26:59,438 --> 00:27:06,596
重大的猜想是测试攀登装备的著名岩石，人们留在
那里是为了捕捉那些偶尔被证明是巨大高峰的时刻。
Big conjectures are famous rocks for testing, climbing gear, and people stay for the rare moment one turns out to be a giant mountain.

228
00:27:07,246 --> 00:27:13,924
Stephen Wolfram 称纯数学是人类最大的智力结构，
是由孤独的攀登者在 2000 多年间建立起来的。
Stephen Wolfram called Pure Math humanity's largest intellectual structure built by lone climbers over 2,000 years.

229
00:27:14,542 --> 00:27:15,808
然后飞机出现了。
Then the airplane shows up.

230
00:27:16,174 --> 00:27:24,132
莱特兄弟的第一次飞行持续了 12 秒，覆盖的距离甚至不如一架客机的翼展，
他认为这正是目前 AI 在数学领域的现状。
The Wright brothers' first flight lasted 12 seconds and covered less distance than an airliner's wingspan,
which he says is about where AI is in math now.

231
00:27:24,590 --> 00:27:33,476
直到今年，这些飞机才勉强离地并耗费巨资，但最近它们已经飞入丛林深处，
并降落在人类从未到达的岩石上。
Until this year, the planes barely got off the ground and cost a fortune, but
lately they've flown deep into the jungle and landed on rocks no human ever reached.

232
00:27:34,030 --> 00:27:40,196
数学家们说那些岩石并不有趣，而且飞机永远无法到达真正的巅峰，他称这种观点是静态思维。
Mathematicians say those rocks weren't interesting and planes will never reach the real peaks, which he calls static thinking.

233
00:27:40,654 --> 00:27:47,332
一旦飞行变得廉价，任何人都可以包机，卫星将绘制出所有的宝藏，到那时情况就会变得混乱。
Once flying gets cheap, anyone can charter a plane, satellites will map every treasure, and it'll be chaotic.

234
00:27:47,918 --> 00:27:57,028
老派探险家会指责大公司破坏丛林，他认为他们是对的，但这改变不了任何事，
因为那些公司会在那里发掘到难以想象的财富。
The old explorers will blame big companies for ruining the jungle, and he says they're right, but it won't change anything,
because those companies will find unimaginable wealth there.

235
00:27:57,582 --> 00:28:03,460
攀登将作为一种爱好保留下来，而数学将变得更出色、更有用，也更平庸。
Climbing survives as a hobby, and math becomes more brilliant, more useful, and more mundane.

236
00:28:03,918 --> 00:28:07,748
他的最后一个章节以四个词开头：不要赌输给飞机。
His last section opens with four words don't bet against airplanes.

237
00:28:08,128 --> 00:28:13,380
任何说 AI 不能产生新想法或自我解释的人，描述的都是去年春天的模型。
Anyone saying AI can't come up with new ideas or explain itself is describing last spring's models.

238
00:28:13,902 --> 00:28:25,220
大学看起来可能没变，但它们将奖励那些有价值的探索选择、指挥 AI 舰队以及向世界解释发现，
他承认很多人会感到被降职并对此抗争。
Universities will look the same, but they'll reward picking what's worth exploring, commanding fleets of AI,
and explaining discoveries to the world, and he admits plenty of people will feel demoted and fight it.

239
00:28:25,486 --> 00:28:34,048
他的结论是，数学即将毕业，离开象牙塔，成为所有科学和技术的基石。
His verdict is that mathematics is about to graduate, leave the Ivory Tower, and become the foundation of all science and technology.

240
00:28:35,150 --> 00:28:39,076
所以这周，Anthropic 发布了一些我诚实说没预料到会这么快就出的内容。
So this week, Anthropic put out something I honestly didn't expect this soon.

241
00:28:39,630 --> 00:28:49,124
他们拿出了 Claude Mythos 5，给它提供八个量子电路的纯文本描述，
再加上一个检查并评分每项设计的自动化程序，基本上就是让它去干活了。
They took Claude Mythos 5, gave it plain language descriptions of eight quantum circuits,
plus an automated program that checks and scores every design, and basically let it go work.

242
00:28:49,614 --> 00:28:57,316
在八个中的七个里，它给出的设计超越了人类发表的最佳结果，
有些情况甚至高出一个数量级或更多。
On seven of the eight, it came back with designs that beat the best ones humans have published,
in some cases by an order of magnitude or more.

243
00:28:57,710 --> 00:29:01,828
而在第八个中，它构建出了文献中根本不存在的东西。
And on the 8th, it built something that just didn't exist in the literature.

244
00:29:02,286 --> 00:29:09,604
关于这事儿有很多过度炒作的噱头，所以让我们来看看实际发生了什么，
再加上本周 Google 的一个与之契合的结果。
There's a lot of overcooked hype around this, so let's go through what actually happened,
plus a Google result from the same week that fits right in.

245
00:29:10,062 --> 00:29:11,140
先说点枯燥的细节。
Quick boring stuff first.

246
00:29:11,598 --> 00:29:16,900
这是来自 Anthropic 的 STEM Fellows 项目，论文于 10 月 15 日在 arXiv 上发布。
This came out of Anthropic's STEM Fellows program, and the paper hit RX5 on October 15th.

247
00:29:17,422 --> 00:29:18,724
它有 46 页。
It's 46 pages.

248
00:29:19,022 --> 00:29:25,092
它的标题是《利用大语言模型发现最先进的量子电路》，我把链接放在下面了。
It's called Discovering State-of-the-art Quantum Circuits with Large Language Models, and I'll leave the link below.

249
00:29:25,550 --> 00:29:28,208
首席作者是 Andy Gu，他是该项目的成员之一。
The lead author is Andy Gu, one of the fellows.

250
00:29:28,580 --> 00:29:35,364
Gu 在量子物理学家 Alec Kemeny 的指导下，并与来自
哈佛大学的 Suzanne Yellen 和 Mikhail Lukin 合作。
Gu was mentored by quantum physicist Alec Kemeny and worked with Suzanne Yellen and Mikhail Lukin from Harvard.

251
00:29:35,758 --> 00:29:41,220
一天后，Anthropic 发布了自己的文章，介绍如何利用 Claude 设计更高效的量子电路。
A day later, Anthropic posted its own write-up, designing more efficient quantum circuits with Claude.

252
00:29:41,488 --> 00:29:43,076
不过有一点要记住。
Just keep one thing in mind though.

253
00:29:43,502 --> 00:29:49,188
你听到的每一个数据都来自 Anthropic 或论文本身，目前还没有人复现过这些结果。
Every number you'll hear comes from Anthropic or the paper itself, and nobody's reproduced any of it yet.

254
00:29:49,646 --> 00:29:50,404
那它是怎么运作的呢？
So how did it work?

255
00:29:50,926 --> 00:29:55,172
Claude 接收到一份关于计算原语的规范，并用 Python 提出一个电路方案。
Claude got a spec for a computational primitive and proposed a circuit in Python.

256
00:29:55,598 --> 00:29:58,404
一个独立的评估器会检查该电路是否正确。
A separate evaluator checked whether the circuit was correct.

257
00:29:58,926 --> 00:30:01,636
这个评估器是一个程序，而不是另一个模型。
That evaluator is a program, not another model.

258
00:30:02,094 --> 00:30:07,588
它根据立方计数乘以门数量来给每个设计打分，这基本上是用来衡量运行时间的指标。
It scored each design on cubic count times gate count, which is basically a stand-in for runtime.

259
00:30:07,822 --> 00:30:13,156
分数传回后，Claude 进行修改，如此循环往复，中间不需要人工干预。
The score goes back, Claude revises, and around it goes, with no human between rounds.

260
00:30:13,710 --> 00:30:16,516
Anthropic 表示 Claude 在很大程度上是自主完成工作的。
Anthropic says Claude worked largely on its own.

261
00:30:17,006 --> 00:30:17,956
有两个因素让它奏效。
Two things make it work.

262
00:30:18,158 --> 00:30:24,996
评估器独立于提议者，所以看起来很像正确的错误设计只会得零分，而不会在辩论中获胜。
The evaluator is independent from the proposer, so a convincing looking wrong design just scores zero instead of winning an argument.

263
00:30:25,550 --> 00:30:29,732
而且目标是一个数值，这样模型就能判断修改是否真的起到了作用。
And the goal is a number, so the model can tell whether a revision actually helped.

264
00:30:30,286 --> 00:30:33,648
它的结构与驱动编程智能体的测试套件相同。
It's the same shape as a test suite driving a coding agent.

265
00:30:34,222 --> 00:30:36,740
这就是为什么 Anthropic 选择量子电路。
And that's why Anthropic picked quantum circuits.

266
00:30:37,358 --> 00:30:40,644
它们自带一种简单、廉价且自动的正确性检查。
They come with a hard, cheap, automatic correctness check.

267
00:30:41,134 --> 00:30:49,924
这八种基础算子涵盖了化学、优化、量子模拟、数论和数值计算，而量子电路有两个奇怪的规则。
The eight primitives span chemistry, optimization, quantum simulation, number
theory, and numerical computing, and quantum circuits have two weird rules.

268
00:30:50,446 --> 00:30:52,868
首先，没有“如果-那么”的分支判断。
First, there's no if-then branching.

269
00:30:53,326 --> 00:31:01,668
普通程序在路线 A 和路线 B 之间做选择，但由于叠加态的存在，
量子电路必须包含每一次运行中所有分支的操作。
A normal program picks Route A or route B, but because of superposition, a
quantum circuit has to include the operations for every branch in every run.

270
00:31:02,286 --> 00:31:04,356
其次，你不能丢弃任何东西。
Second, you can't throw anything away.

271
00:31:04,750 --> 00:31:09,604
每一步都必须是可逆的，因此擦除中间变量会污染结果。
Every step must be reversible, so erasing scratch values contaminates the result.

272
00:31:09,966 --> 00:31:14,980
唯一的清理方法是进行“反计算”，即反向运行计算过程，但这会消耗量子门。
The only way to clean up is to uncompute, run the calculation backwards, which costs gates.

273
00:31:15,662 --> 00:31:20,132
这迫使在量子比特与步骤之间进行权衡，而这在经典计算中没有真正的对应物。
That forces a qubits versus steps trade-off with no real classical equivalent.

274
00:31:20,654 --> 00:31:22,724
这正是可以交给搜索算法去解决的问题。
Exactly the kind of thing you can point a search at.

275
00:31:23,310 --> 00:31:26,564
压缩电路非常重要，因为目前的硬件还很不成熟。
Squeezing circuits matters because the hardware is still rough.

276
00:31:27,054 --> 00:31:31,908
现在的机器只有几百到几千个量子比特，而且它们极其脆弱。
Today's machines have a few hundred to a few thousand qubits, and they're super fragile.

277
00:31:32,334 --> 00:31:40,068
一点热量、轻微的震动甚至宇宙射线都会导致错误，一旦这些错误堆积，结果就没用了。
A bit of heat, a slight vibration, even cosmic rays can cause errors, and once those pile up, the result is useless.

278
00:31:40,718 --> 00:31:49,220
因此，要实现破解加密、研发新药或室温超导体等目
标，意味着必须尽可能减少使用的量子比特和时间。
So getting to things like breaking encryption, new drugs, or room temperature
superconductors means using as few qubits and as little time as possible.

279
00:31:49,582 --> 00:31:51,300
好的，现在看核心成果。
Okay, the headline result.

280
00:31:51,694 --> 00:31:56,164
它被称为 除法步骤，是关于素数域模逆的算法。
It's called div steps, and it's about prime field modular inversion.

281
00:31:56,462 --> 00:32:01,604
椭圆曲线数学广泛应用于密码学，其中有一个核心步骤叫“点加”。
Elliptic curve math is all over cryptography, and it has a core step called point addition.

282
00:32:02,094 --> 00:32:06,020
在点加中，成本最高的运算是模逆。
The most expensive operation inside point addition is modular inversion.

283
00:32:06,446 --> 00:32:16,484
经典计算机通过 除法步骤 来快速完成它，该算法不断进行交换、相加或相减，
并对两个数进行折半，同时生成分支信息并直接丢弃。
Classical computers do it fast with div steps, which keeps swapping, adding, or subtracting, and halving two numbers,
generating branch information along the way and just tossing it.

284
00:32:16,942 --> 00:32:18,884
但量子计算机不能丢弃这些信息。
A quantum computer can't toss it.

285
00:32:19,086 --> 00:32:27,536
你必须存储所有的分支历史，但这会消耗大量的量子比特，
因此 除法步骤 在可逆整数算术中被认为不切实际。
You'd have to store the whole branch history, which eats an absurd number of qubits,
so div steps was considered impractical for reversible integer arithmetic.

286
00:32:27,790 --> 00:32:33,988
Claude 的思路是：好，如果你不存储历史记录，而是从最终结果反推出来呢？
Claude's angle was, okay, what if you don't store the history and just work it back out from the final results?

287
00:32:34,638 --> 00:32:39,588
起初，它猜测了一系列规则，但一旦涉及到 256 位数字，这些规则就崩溃了。
At first, it guessed at a bunch of rules, which fell apart once it hit 256-bit numbers.

288
00:32:39,982 --> 00:32:52,964
于是它放弃了暴力测试，转而进行真正的数学推导。它研究了 除法步骤 迭代的演变过程，
证明了一系列新的代数恒等式，据此写出了精确的解码规则，并在 lean 中进行了形式化验证。
So it dropped brute force testing and did actual math. It studied how the div steps iterations evolve,
proved a set of new algebraic identities, wrote an exact decoding rule from them, and formally verified it in lean.

289
00:32:53,422 --> 00:32:57,732
这是第一个不需要存储分支历史的可逆 除法步骤 实现。
That's the first reversible div steps implementation with no stored branch history.

290
00:32:58,190 --> 00:33:08,740
与其说这是一个单一的胜利，不如说是一个帕累托转变——一系列的新设计，
其中一种设计虽然比之前的最小设计多用 12% 的量子比特，但减少了 17 倍的门数量。
It's less a single win than a Pareto shift, a whole family of designs, where one
uses 12% more qubits but 17 times fewer gates than the smallest previous design.

291
00:33:09,230 --> 00:33:13,476
因此，拥有充足量子比特预算的编译器现在可以将其转化为更少的门数。
So, a compiler with qubit budget to spare can now trade it for gates.

292
00:33:14,158 --> 00:33:20,324
Point Edition 也取得了自己的成果，仅通过一个初始简报和偶尔的提示词，
就完成了一次持续 53 小时的运行。
Point Edition got its own result too, from a single 53-hour run with just an initial brief and the occasional prompt.

293
00:33:20,750 --> 00:33:32,612
Claude 找到了一种新方法，证明了代数恒等式，在大型数值模拟中测试了公式，
并在 lean 中将主张正式化，这让它不再仅仅是看起来合理的推测。
Claude found a new approach, proved the algebraic identities, tested the formulas in large-scale numerical simulations,
and formalized the claim in lean, which makes it hard to dismiss as just plausible looking.

294
00:33:33,294 --> 00:33:36,068
DQI 这个大概是我最喜欢的。
The DQI one is probably my favorite.

295
00:33:36,558 --> 00:33:39,696
解码量子干涉测量是一种优化算法。
Decoding quantum interferometry is an optimization algorithm.

296
00:33:39,856 --> 00:33:47,108
人们常指出的物流、调度和材料设计，其中最昂贵的一步是 Reed-Solomon 解码器。
People point at things like logistics, scheduling, and material design, and its most expensive step is a Reed-Solomon decoder.

297
00:33:47,534 --> 00:33:56,164
谷歌之前的构建使用的是扩展欧几里德算法，由于电路不能分支，
它必须跨越大量的轮次进行拉伸。
Google's previous construction used the extended Euclidean algorithm, and since circuits can't branch,
it had to be stretched over a huge number of rounds.

298
00:33:56,782 --> 00:34:04,580
Claude 基本判定这不符合量子电路，转而采用
Burlicamp Massey 解码，它在每一轮中执行相同的操作。
Claude basically decided that doesn't fit quantum circuits and switched
to Burlicamp Massey decoding, which does the same operation every round.

299
00:34:04,942 --> 00:34:07,012
不过，这产生了一个内存问题。
That created a memory problem, though.

300
00:34:07,438 --> 00:34:16,900
每一轮都会留下需要稍后回溯的临时数据，处理所有
35 轮中的最坏情况异常将需要 665 个量子比特。
Every round leaves temporary data you need later to rewind, and handling
worst case exceptions across all 35 rounds would take 665 qubits.

301
00:34:17,518 --> 00:34:23,043
所以它利用了“同等工作反向操作”的技巧来消除大部分存储空间，只留下一些离群值。
So it used the same work it backwards trick to kill most of the storage, leaving a few outliers.

302
00:34:23,661 --> 00:34:27,012
稳妥的做法还是为这些情况预留大量空间。
The safe move would be to reserve lots of space for those anyway.

303
00:34:27,438 --> 00:34:35,331
相反，Claude 为自己写了一个快速模拟器，并运行
了 4.03 亿次采样解码，以查看离群值出现的频率。
Instead, Claude wrote itself a fast simulator and ran 403 million sample decodings to see how often outliers show up.

304
00:34:35,552 --> 00:34:38,116
绝大多数情况下，一个数值就足够了。
Almost always, a single value is enough.

305
00:34:38,606 --> 00:34:49,476
所以它只为那部分预留了空间，即 19 个量子比特，并接受大约
万分之一的运行需要更多资源并失败，这在允许的误差预算内。
So it reserved room for just that, 19 qubits, and accepted that roughly one
run in 10,000 needs more and fails, which is inside the allowed error budget.

306
00:34:49,902 --> 00:34:53,219
最终结果是，比谷歌的解码器少用了 12 倍的门。
End result, 12 times fewer gates than Google's decoder.

307
00:34:53,678 --> 00:35:06,116
而且 Google Quantum AI 自己的估算表明，一个 OPI 问题在 Frontier 超级计算机上大约需要
三个月，而运行 DQI 的未来量子计算机仅需约一小时。
And Google Quantum AI's own estimates suggest one OPI problem would take about three months on the Frontier supercomputer versus
roughly an hour on a future quantum computer running DQI.

308
00:35:06,670 --> 00:35:15,620
那一个小时的大部分时间都花在 Reed-Solomon 解码上，因此减少 12 倍影响了主项，
某些覆盖范围将其转化为将那一小时缩短到几分钟。
Most of that hour is spent on Reed Solomon decoding, so a 12 times cut hits the dominant term,
which some coverage translates into that hour becoming a few minutes.

309
00:35:16,302 --> 00:35:18,112
现在，进入被过度炒作的部分。
Now, the overhyped part.

310
00:35:18,318 --> 00:35:25,412
大家都在引用 Femoco，这是固氮酶核心的铁钼辅因子，是生产肥料的关键。
Everyone's quoting Femoco, the iron molybdenum cofactor at the core of nitrogenase, which is key to fertilizer production.

311
00:35:25,806 --> 00:35:30,372
2017 年，模拟它的估算约为 50 万亿个 toffoli 门。
In 2017, the estimate to simulate it was about 50 trillion tofoli gates.

312
00:35:30,832 --> 00:35:35,492
现在大约是 3.4 亿，下降了约 15 万倍。
Now it's around 340 million, roughly 150,000-fold drop.

313
00:35:35,950 --> 00:35:41,860
Anthropic 的页面显示，在拥有约 300 万个物理量子比特的未来机器上，这只需要几个小时。
Anthropic's page says that works out to a few hours on a future machine with about 3 million physical qubits.

314
00:35:42,510 --> 00:35:48,644
新华社报道称，人类耗时八年，而 Claude 只用了 53 小时。
Chinese outlet Xinhuan ran that as humans took eight years, Claude took 53 hours.

315
00:35:49,102 --> 00:35:50,276
事实并非如此。
That's not what happened.

316
00:35:50,702 --> 00:36:02,052
Anthropic 的页面明确表示，8 年的跨度归功于许多研究小组，
所以 Claude 的设计只是已经大幅下降的曲线上的一个步骤，而 53 小时是椭圆曲线运行的时间。
Anthropic's own page credits the 8-year drop to many research groups, so Claude's design is one step on a curve that was already
falling steeply, and the 53 hours was the elliptic curve run.

317
00:36:02,510 --> 00:36:08,352
同一篇报道还称 Claude 在所有八项任务中获胜，而实际上是七个更好的分数加上一个新的表述。
The same piece also said Claude won all eight tasks when it's seven better scores plus one new formulation.

318
00:36:08,558 --> 00:36:10,852
无论如何，网络上的反响非常热烈。
The reaction online was huge anyway.

319
00:36:11,086 --> 00:36:19,396
有人开玩笑说，每个物理博士都意识到 AI 可以将
他们多年的工作从纯文字重写成好 10 倍的内容。
One person joked that every physics PhD just realized an AI can rewrite
their years of work from plain language into something 10 times better.

320
00:36:19,822 --> 00:36:28,164
还有人说我们将提前数年获得实用的量子机器，或者
说 AI 从解释科学变成了发现我们尚未理解的事物。
Others said we'll get useful quantum machines years early, or that AI went
from explaining science to discovering things we don't understand yet.

321
00:36:28,654 --> 00:36:36,964
这听起来很戏剧性，当然，但即使是谨慎的报告也承认该方法值得认真对待，
只要这些倍数仍标注为 Anthropic 自有的数据。
Dramatic, sure, but even the careful write-ups say the method deserves to be taken seriously,
as long as the multipliers stay labeled as Anthropic's own.

322
00:36:37,486 --> 00:36:49,750
在有人脱离语境引用那 17 倍之前，我们要看清限制：Anthropic 运行了评估器，
而基准来自论文自带的表格，包含 Schrotenlower 2026、
Now the limits, before anyone quotes that 17 times out of context, Anthropic ran the evaluator,
and the baselines come from the paper's own tables, with prior designs from

323
00:36:49,750 --> 00:36:50,480
在有人脱离语境引用那 17 倍之前，我们要看清限制：Anthropic 运行了评估器，
而基准来自论文自带的表格，包含 Schrotenlower 2026、
Schrotenlower 2026, Luo and Colleagues 2026, and Qatar and Colleagues 2025.

324
00:36:50,480 --> 00:36:55,332
Luo 和同事 2026 以及 Qatar 和同事 2025 的先前设计。
Schrotenlower 2026, Luo and Colleagues 2026, and Qatar and Colleagues 2025.

325
00:36:55,822 --> 00:36:58,724
在有人重新运行评测框架之前，这目前只是一个声明。
Until somebody reruns the harness, it's a claim.

326
00:36:59,150 --> 00:37:03,076
Anthropic 还报告了模型自身的失败模式，这一点我很欣赏。
Anthropic also reported a failure mode against itself, which I respect.

327
00:37:03,406 --> 00:37:05,348
在早期阶段，模型的表现过于保守。
Early on, the model was too conservative.

328
00:37:06,030 --> 00:37:12,324
它不断质疑那些有充分依据的收益，并且对原本没问题的设计反复确认好几次。
It kept second-guessing well-supported gains and double or triple checking designs that were probably fine.

329
00:37:12,590 --> 00:37:16,964
这种谨慎在某种程度上是有回报的，因为它促成了 Lean 在除法步骤上的证明。
That caution paid off once because it's what prompted the lean proofs on div steps.

330
00:37:17,582 --> 00:37:20,932
但总体而言，它让搜索偏向于那些成熟的方法。
But overall, it biased the search toward established approaches.

331
00:37:21,230 --> 00:37:28,100
修复方案是结构性的：同时采用几种性质不同的并行方法，
并偶尔加入一些提示词来扩大搜索范围。
The fix was structural, several qualitatively different approaches in parallel, plus the occasional nudge to widen the search.

332
00:37:28,526 --> 00:37:35,492
任何在前沿模型上构建评估循环的人可能都遇到过这个问题，而这种并行技巧是值得借鉴的部分。
Anyone building evaluator loops on frontier models has probably hit this, and the parallel trick is the part worth stealing.

333
00:37:35,982 --> 00:37:45,316
而且论文本身将那个新的公式视为真正的收获，因为
如果搜索只是在已知结构内调整参数，就会遇到瓶颈。
And the paper itself treats that one new formulation as the real prize, because
a search that only tunes parameters inside a known structure has a ceiling.

334
00:37:45,774 --> 00:37:50,052
去掉物理层面的限制，你就得到了一个提议者和一个共享评分的独立检查者。
Strip the physics out, and you've got a proposer and an independent checker sharing a score.

335
00:37:50,272 --> 00:37:52,832
这是目前严肃的智能体工作的标准架构。
The standard shape of serious agent work now.

336
00:37:53,072 --> 00:37:56,068
当测试通过时就停止，而不是看输出读起来顺不顺。
You stop when a test passes, not when the output reads well.

337
00:37:56,526 --> 00:37:58,020
而且这里的评论者是客观的。
And the critic here is honest.

338
00:37:58,382 --> 00:38:03,076
它不是一个有主观偏好的模型，而是一个接受或拒绝电路的模拟器。
It's not a model with an opinion, it's a simulator that accepts the circuit or doesn't.

339
00:38:03,534 --> 00:38:07,908
当程序无法判断时，最好的替代方案就是用另一个模型作为裁判。
When a program can't judge, the next best thing is a different model as judge.

340
00:38:08,366 --> 00:38:09,156
Orca Router。
Orca Router.

341
00:38:09,392 --> 00:38:14,788
这是一个路由服务，它发布了关于将此类框架视为路由问题的详细分析。
A router service that published one of the more detailed breakdowns of this frames that as a routing problem.

342
00:38:15,246 --> 00:38:21,988
你可以用廉价模型处理高频率的提议，而只在验证环节使用更强的模型，
或者让一组模型对同一个提示词进行评审。
You put a cheap model on the high volume proposing and a stronger one only on verifying, or you run a panel of models on one prompt.

343
00:38:22,286 --> 00:38:25,552
所有这些都在一个端点上运行，涵盖了超过 200 个模型。
All of that runs across more than 200 models on one endpoint.

344
00:38:26,094 --> 00:38:34,372
显然，没有任何路由系统设计了这些电路，但重现这些过程
意味着每个基础组件都要经过数百轮的提议、评估和修改。
No router designed these circuits, obviously, but reproducing this means hundreds of propose evaluate revise rounds per primitive.

345
00:38:34,862 --> 00:38:40,804
因此他们主张采用自动故障转移，而不是把长达
12 小时的搜索押注在某个供应商偶尔表现良好上。
So they argue for automatic failover instead of betting a 12-hour search on one provider having a good afternoon.

346
00:38:41,262 --> 00:38:49,508
他们还运行一个 AI 事件存档，其中每一个记录的失败
都会标注来源、严重程度、置信度等级以及争议标记。
They also run an AI incident archive where each documented failure gets sources, severity, a confidence grade, and a disputed flag.

347
00:38:49,998 --> 00:38:52,132
你无法使用 Mythos 5 本身。
Mythos 5 itself you can't use.

348
00:38:52,494 --> 00:38:57,632
它仅限于经过认证的合作伙伴和验证计划成员，不在任何公共 API 上提供。
It's limited to vetted partners and verification program members, nowhere on a public API.

349
00:38:57,902 --> 00:39:01,668
Anthropic 将每一个前沿步骤作为相同权重的两个版本发布。
Anthropic ships each frontier step as two versions of the same weights.

350
00:39:02,286 --> 00:39:08,964
Mythos 为经过认证的防御者调整了网络和生物安全防护，而 Fable 则开启了完整的防护堆栈。
Mythos has cyber and biology safeguards tuned for vetted defenders, and Fable has the full safeguard stack on.

351
00:39:09,454 --> 00:39:19,620
因此公共选项是 Clawed Fable 5，每百万输入标记 10 美元，每百万输出 50 美元，
Orca Router 在转发时不加任何额外费用。
So the public option is Clawed Fable 5, at $10 per million input tokens and $50 per million output,
which Orca Router passes through at zero markup.

352
00:39:20,078 --> 00:39:27,652
Fable 5.1 是 Mythos 5.1 的公共孪生版本，价格相同，但缓存读取成本降低了 75%。
Fable 5.1, the public twin of Mythos 5.1, costs the same with a 75% cheaper cash read.

353
00:39:28,142 --> 00:39:37,604
它拥有 100 万 token 的上下文窗口，128,000 的最大输出，
且首个 token 的平均耗时为 3.72 秒。
It has a 1 million token context window, 128,000 max output, and a median time to first token of 3.72 seconds.

354
00:39:38,222 --> 00:39:42,084
我关注的是关于除法步骤和 DQI 的独立重复测试。
What I'm watching for is an independent rerun on div steps and DQI.

355
00:39:42,318 --> 00:39:48,772
我还想看看评测框架是否会被发布，因为循环是可重用的部分，而电路更像是演示内容。
I also want to see whether the harness gets released, since the loop is the reusable part and the circuits are kind of the demo.

356
00:39:49,294 --> 00:39:52,836
而且我想看看这种模式是否也会出现在无法通过机器校验的正确性问题上。
And I want to see whether this pattern shows up where correctness can't be machine checked.

357
00:39:53,072 --> 00:39:55,460
最后一个限制，正好可以顺势转到下一个话题。
One last limit, and it's a perfect segue.

358
00:39:55,822 --> 00:40:01,316
电路设计是量子计算机的一个组成部分，而且这些部件通常是分开设计的。
Circuit design is one piece of a quantum computer, and the pieces are usually designed separately.

359
00:40:01,806 --> 00:40:09,540
Anthropic 提到了通过联合优化纠错、编译和硬件来
提升性能，但这只是一个研究方向，而不是最终结果。
Anthropic floats, optimizing error correction, compilation, and hardware jointly, but that's a research direction, not a result.

360
00:40:10,126 --> 00:40:14,596
而纠错正是 Google 在 10 月 15 日取得重大突破的地方。
An error correction is exactly where Google landed something big on October 15th.

361
00:40:15,118 --> 00:40:28,580
Google Quantum AI 的研究科学家 Emma Rosenfeld 和量子软件工程师 Craig Gidney 宣布，
魔法状态培育在他们的 Willow 处理器上已具备实践可行性，能减少约 40 倍的错误。
Emma Rosenfeld, a research scientist at Google Quantum AI, and Craig Gidney, a quantum software engineer there,
announced that Magic State Cultivation works in practice on their Willow processor, cutting errors about 40 times.

362
00:40:28,878 --> 00:40:30,116
这项成果已发表在《科学》杂志上。
It's published in Science.

363
00:40:30,798 --> 00:40:41,636
为了实现通用量子计算，你需要运行并纠正一系列超越经典计算能力的特定操作，
而这些操作首先需要通过制造所谓的“魔法状态”来获得。
For universal quantum computing, you need to run and error correct, a specific set of operations that take you beyond classical,
and you get them by first making so-called magic states.

364
00:40:42,286 --> 00:40:46,884
问题在于，高质量的、经过纠错的魔法状态成本极其高昂。
The catch is that good error-corrected magic states are brutally expensive.

365
00:40:47,438 --> 00:40:54,180
一些估计称，量子计算机高达 95% 的能力可能都要消
耗在生产这些状态上，而且一旦使用，它就会消失。
Some estimates say up to 95% of a quantum computer's capacity could go into producing them, and once you use one, it's gone.

366
00:40:54,670 --> 00:41:03,012
研究人员早在 2004 年就预见到了这一点，那时量子计算还不是真正的工程学，
他们花了 20 年时间在不断攻克这个难题。
Researchers saw this coming in 2004, long before quantum computing was real engineering, and have spent 20 years chipping away at it.

367
00:41:03,470 --> 00:41:10,372
2024 年，Gidney、Noah Shuddy 和 Cody Jones 将文献中的一个想法完善成了“培育”技术。
In 2024, Gidney, Noah Shuddy, and Cody Jones refined an idea from the literature into cultivation.

368
00:41:10,638 --> 00:41:11,844
它的工作原理就像一个过滤器。
It works like a filter.

369
00:41:12,270 --> 00:41:20,292
你将一个带噪声的状态注入到芯片的一个小区域，并
运行高度协同的测量来捕捉错误，剔除掉失败的尝试。
You inject a noisy state into a small region of the chip and run tightly
coordinated measurements to catch errors, throwing out flawed attempts.

370
00:41:20,974 --> 00:41:27,140
剩下的部分会成长为一个非常纯净的状态，同时它也会被适配成更大、更有用的编码。
What's left grows into a really pure state, and at the same time it gets adapted into a larger, useful encoding.

371
00:41:27,472 --> 00:41:31,236
从理论上讲，这能显著缩小执行实际任务所需的机器规模。
On paper, that could seriously shrink the machine you'd need for practical tasks.

372
00:41:31,950 --> 00:41:33,232
但要把它变成现实却更难。
Making it real was harder.

373
00:41:33,486 --> 00:41:37,124
Rosenfeld 一直看到一些似乎违反物理定律的数据。
Rosenfeld kept seeing data that seemed to break the laws of physics.

374
00:41:37,774 --> 00:41:46,916
在经历了数月的困惑、模拟、与同事讨论以及一致性检查后，
她发现这是由于团队常用的测量技术中存在一个错误的假设。
After months of confusion, simulations, talks with colleagues, and consistency checks,
she traced it to a wrong assumption in the team's go-to measurement technique.

375
00:41:47,502 --> 00:41:52,356
来自电气设备漂移和温度变化的噪声破坏了基准测试。
Noise from electrical equipment drift and temperature variation was undermining the benchmark.

376
00:41:52,718 --> 00:41:55,492
于是他们在理论和工程上都进行了调整。
So they pivoted on both theory and engineering.

377
00:41:55,950 --> 00:42:02,500
他们增加了额外的控制来减少那种噪声，并发明了一
种利用“培育”技术进行自我测量的全新基准测试方法。
They added extra control to reduce that noise and invented a new benchmarking technique that uses cultivation to measure itself.

378
00:42:02,958 --> 00:42:10,192
这刷新了量子计量学的最先进标准，T-States 的逻辑保真度达到了创纪录的 99.99%。
That set a new state-of-the-art in quantum metrology, with T-States at a record logical fidelity of 99.99%.

379
00:42:11,022 --> 00:42:16,420
这是该领域最严重的资源瓶颈之一，首次在硬件上实现了实用的解决方案。
It's the first real hardware demonstration of a practical fix for one of the field's worst resource bottlenecks.

380
00:42:17,070 --> 00:42:22,820
他们还将来自距离 3 颜色码的状态嫁接到距离 5 表面码上。
They also grafted states from a distance 3 color code onto a distance 5 surface code.

381
00:42:23,310 --> 00:42:30,192
颜色码是一种较新的纠错方案，非常适合用于培育，而表面码是更成熟的方法。
Color codes are a newer error correction scheme that's ideal for cultivation, and surface codes are the more established method.

382
00:42:30,478 --> 00:42:32,708
纯化后的状态能够顺利完成转换。
The purified states survive the transfer.

383
00:42:33,134 --> 00:42:41,892
它仍需在更大规模上运行，而且在 Google 获得能解决那些原
本无法解决问题的实用纠错机器之前，还有许多挑战要克服。
It still has to work at larger scale, and plenty of challenges remain before
Google gets its useful error corrected machine for otherwise unsolvable problems.

384
00:42:43,854 --> 00:42:46,948
Anthropic 最神秘的模型刚刚提前流出。
Anthropic's most mysterious model just slipped out early.

385
00:42:47,438 --> 00:42:54,370
Claude Mythos 5.5 已经列在 Azure 上了，参数也泄露了，
你们中的一些人可能在不知情的情况下就在使用它，而且人
Claude Fable 5.5 is already listed on Azure, the specs leaked, some of you might be using it without even knowing,
and people are building full games, animated films, even a symphony with it.

386
00:42:54,370 --> 00:42:57,988
们正用它来制作完整的游戏、动画电影，甚至还有交响乐。
Claude Fable 5.5 is already listed on Azure, the specs leaked, some of you might be using it without even knowing,
and people are building full games, animated films, even a symphony with it.

387
00:42:58,478 --> 00:43:02,948
有人认为 AI 基本就是构建了它，而且关于 Opus 6 的传闻已经传开了。
Some think AI basically built it, and Opus 6 rumors are already flying.

388
00:43:03,438 --> 00:43:06,496
此外，Opus 5.5 的速度变得更快，成本也更低了。
Plus, Opus 5.5 got way faster and cheaper.

389
00:43:06,766 --> 00:43:14,724
Claude 学会了不再浪费你的 Token，OpenAI 正在准备反
击，而 Meta 回到了开源阵营，甚至还和苹果公司联手了。
Claude learned to stop wasting your tokens, OpenAI's lining up a counterpunch,
and Meta's back in open source, teamed up with Apple of all companies.

390
00:43:15,438 --> 00:43:19,616
好，先说 Fable，因为 Anthropic 官方并没有正式宣布它。
Okay, Fable first, because nobody at Anthropic actually announced it.

391
00:43:19,854 --> 00:43:22,116
开发者只是在配置文件里发现了它。
Developers just found it sitting in a config file.

392
00:43:22,606 --> 00:43:35,012
一个通过 Light LLM 同步的代码提交显示，Azure 的 EastUS 2 模型目录中出现了一个全新的
ID：Azure.ai/Claude Fable55，状态为“正式发布”。
A code submission synced by lightllm showed a brand new ID in Azure's EastUS 2
model directory, Azure.ai slash Claude Fable55, with the status generally available.

393
00:43:35,438 --> 00:43:37,188
还记得 Fable 5.1 吗？
Remember Fable 5.1?

394
00:43:37,422 --> 00:43:41,924
它在 Bedrock 上上线后，仅仅一天就对网络上的普通用户开放了。
It got listed on Bedrock and one day later it was open to regular users on the web.

395
00:43:42,318 --> 00:43:45,988
所以全面发布可能就在眼前，甚至可能就在这周。
So the full release is probably around the corner, maybe even this week.

396
00:43:46,542 --> 00:43:49,668
不过并不是所有人都相信，怀疑论者也有他们的道理。
Not everyone's buying it yet, though, and the skeptics have a point.

397
00:43:50,222 --> 00:43:58,468
Light LLM 是开源的，所以它的配置与 Azure 目录同步完全正常，不被视为第二个独立来源。
Light LLM is open source, so its config syncing with the Azure directory is totally normal,
and it doesn't count as a second independent source.

398
00:43:59,086 --> 00:44:02,724
而且，一个显示为 GA 的目录并不意味着今天就会有官方公告。
And a directory saying GA doesn't mean an announcement is coming today.

399
00:44:03,086 --> 00:44:06,308
有人建议不要急着充值账户。
One person's advice don't rush to top up your account.

400
00:44:06,798 --> 00:44:07,844
参数也泄露了。
The specs leak too.

401
00:44:08,110 --> 00:44:18,180
100 万 Token 的上下文窗口，12.8 万的最大输出，以及每百万输入 Token 10 美元、
每百万输出 50 美元的 API 价格。
A 1 million token context window, 128,000 max output, and API pricing of $10 per million input tokens and $50 per million output.

402
00:44:18,606 --> 00:44:21,380
公平地说，这些数据本身并不新奇。
To be fair, none of those numbers are new on their own.

403
00:44:21,806 --> 00:44:30,596
Gemini 在 2024 年就有 100 万的上下文，而 GPT-5 去年就已经能提供 12.8 万的输出了。
Gemini had a million token context back in 2024, and GPT-5 was already doing 128,000 output last year.

404
00:44:31,182 --> 00:44:45,956
尽管如此，单次响应中 12.8 万个 Token 基本相当于一部长篇小说或中型项目的全部代码库，
因此处理长文档和持续运行的复杂代理正是这个模型的核心用途。
Still, 128,000 tokens in one response is basically a full-length novel or the entire code base of a medium-sized project,
so long documents and complex agents running nonstop are exactly what this thing is built for.

405
00:44:46,382 --> 00:44:47,460
问题在于成本。
The catch is cost.

406
00:44:47,918 --> 00:44:55,204
一条评论说，考虑到它消耗的资源，Fable 5.5 必须非常出色才能证明其优于 Opus 的价值。
One comment said Fable 5.5 has to be really excellent to justify using it over Opus, given how much usage it burns.

407
00:44:55,790 --> 00:45:01,732
如果你是没有 API 权限的普通订阅用户，几个长提示词就可能耗尽你 5 小时的配额。
If you're a regular subscriber without API access, a few long prompts could wipe out your 5-hour quota.

408
00:45:02,222 --> 00:45:09,156
所以在早期阶段，现实点说，只有愿意为每百万 Token
支付超过 50 美元的企业客户才用得起这个东西。
So early on, realistically, only enterprise clients willing to pay over 50 bucks per million tokens can afford this thing.

409
00:45:09,614 --> 00:45:14,256
Opus、Sonnet 和 Haiku 5.5 已经发布并表现出色。
Opus, Sonnet, and Haiku 5.5 are already out and doing great.

410
00:45:14,670 --> 00:45:21,316
Fable 是最后一块拼图，是该系列中定位最特殊、能力最难预测的一个。
Fable is the last puzzle piece, the one with the most unusual positioning and the hardest-to-predict capabilities in the series.

411
00:45:21,902 --> 00:45:26,116
一旦它上线，Anthropic 就覆盖了当前市场的方方面面。
Once it lands, Anthropic covers the whole current market, top to bottom.

412
00:45:26,638 --> 00:45:30,180
而且这个时机看起来不像巧合，更像是一场伏击。
And the timing doesn't look like a coincidence, it looks like an ambush.

413
00:45:30,542 --> 00:45:36,324
Argon 迎来了它的高光时刻，而在热度还没退去之前，Fable 就准备好夺走所有的关注点。
Argon gets its day, and before the hype even fades, Fable is lined up to steal the spotlight.

414
00:45:36,718 --> 00:45:49,668
一位 KOL 表示，Anthropic 是 AI 领域最无情、策略计算最周密的公司，
他们不断压制竞争对手并抢占风头，似乎决心在 IPO 前一直保持领先。
One KOL said, Anthropic is the most ruthless, strategically calculating company in AI,
that they keep suppressing competitors and grabbing the limelight and seem determined to stay ahead all the way to their IPO.

415
00:45:50,030 --> 00:45:52,196
业内人士认为这正是重点。
Industry folks think that's exactly the point.

416
00:45:52,590 --> 00:45:54,884
在上市前有更多的缓冲期来积累势头。
More runway to build momentum before going public.

417
00:45:55,342 --> 00:45:57,456
OpenAI 这边也没闲着。
OpenAI's not sitting still either.

418
00:45:57,710 --> 00:46:10,980
据 Synthwaved 的业内人士透露，他们计划在本月为期 28 天的发布活动中全力推广 6.1 Astra，
尽管有传言称 Astra 在未能通过安全评估后曾被推迟。
According to Industry Insider at Synthwaved, they plan to push 6.1 Astra hard during their 28 days of shipping event this month,
although there are rumors Astra was postponed earlier after failing a security assessment.

419
00:46:11,566 --> 00:46:17,732
无论如何，现在竞争非常激烈，人们已经在开玩笑了：享受你短暂的聚光灯时刻吧，小 Argon。
Either way, things are white hot, and people are already joking, enjoy your short time in the spotlight, little Argon.

420
00:46:18,222 --> 00:46:28,420
几天前，敏锐的用户注意到 Claude Opus 5.5 似乎在偷偷将
一些极其复杂的提示词路由到某个神秘且更强大的模型上。
A few days ago, sharp-eyed users noticed Claude Opus 5.5 seemed to be
secretly routing really hard prompts to some mysterious, more powerful model.

421
00:46:28,846 --> 00:46:37,732
这与有关 Fable 5.5 已进入早期预览的报道相吻合，目前
已向部分公司和个人开放，仅剩最后的公开发布前的测试。
That fits with reports that Fable 5.5 is already in early access, Gray released to
some companies and individuals with only final testing left before public launch.

422
00:46:37,998 --> 00:46:40,548
甚至有人找到了一种检查你是否在其中的方法。
People even figured out a way to check if you're in.

423
00:46:40,846 --> 00:46:44,836
开启 Opus 5.5 高级模式并输入：你知道 Voxelbench 吗？
Turn on Opus 5.5 high and type do you know voxel bench?

424
00:46:45,056 --> 00:46:45,696
不要搜索。
Don't search.

425
00:46:45,934 --> 00:46:49,924
然后问：你知道 @legit_api 吗，不要搜索。
Then do you know at legit underscore API, don't search.

426
00:46:50,222 --> 00:46:55,620
Opus 5.5 的知识截止日期较早，所以通常情况下它无法回答这两个问题。
Opus 5.5 has an earlier knowledge cutoff, so normally it can't answer either.

427
00:46:56,046 --> 00:47:10,628
但如果你被路由到了新模型，它会告诉你 Voxelbench 是一个让大模型生成三维体素的空间推理
基准测试，而 @legit_api 是专门报道未发布模型消息的博主。
But if you've been routed to the new model, it'll tell you Voxelbench is a spatial reasoning benchmark where LLMs generate three
dimensional voxels, and at legit underscore API is a blogger who specifically breaks news on unreleased models.

428
00:47:11,406 --> 00:47:15,844
那么，这个东西——极有可能是 Fable 5.5——到底能做什么？
So, what can this thing, most likely Fable 5.5, actually do?

429
00:47:16,270 --> 00:47:21,540
有人说它在五小时内构建了一个完整的、可玩的 MMORPG。
One person said it built a complete, playable MMORPG in five hours.

430
00:47:21,872 --> 00:47:25,124
地图、角色、交互，全部通过代码实现。
Maps, characters, interactions, all through code.

431
00:47:25,614 --> 00:47:38,724
还有人要求它解释 OpenAI 关于准黎曼猜想的 199 页证明，结果它不是给出了解释，
而是写出了渲染一段长达数分钟的三维动画视频的代码。
Another asked it to explain OpenAI's 199-page proof of the quasi-Riemann hypothesis, and instead of an explanation,
it wrote code that rendered a three-dimensional animated video several minutes long.

432
00:47:39,022 --> 00:47:43,460
甚至有人给它扔了一个超过 160 页的纳维-斯托克斯方程证明。
Someone even threw a 160-plus page Navier Stokes proof at it.

433
00:47:43,918 --> 00:47:48,548
真正引起轰动的是来自 @NFT_Chin 的内容。
The one that really blew up came from at NFT underscore Chin.

434
00:47:49,006 --> 00:47:58,852
在 Claude Code 中，该模型基本上变成了一位导演，花了两个半小时写出一段具有诗意、
有点王家卫风格的动画，几乎全部是用代码实现的。
In Claude Code, the model basically became a director and spent two and a half hours writing a poetic,
kind of Wong Kar Wai style animation, almost entirely in code.

435
00:47:59,342 --> 00:48:10,916
它呈现了一个手绘笔触开场，包含中、英、日三语
字幕，纯红背景配白字显示：所以我打破了诺言；
It came up with a hand-drawn brushstroke opening, trilingual subtitles in Chinese, English, and Japanese,
a pure red background with white text reading, so I broke my promise;

436
00:48:11,278 --> 00:48:20,356
等轴测平台的距离标签、色彩鲜艳的条纹建筑分镜
图、穿过铁路轨道，以及纸艺拼贴风格的角色文件。
distance labels on isometric platforms, storyboards of colorful striped
buildings, crossing railway tracks, and paper collage style character files.

437
00:48:20,942 --> 00:48:30,212
这一切都建立在《秒速5厘米》的意境之上，而且风格、节奏、分镜，
每一项艺术决策都是 AI 自行做出的。
It's all built on the imagery of 5 centimeters per second and the style, rhythm, storyboards,
every single art direction call the AI made on its own.

438
00:48:30,670 --> 00:48:37,156
大家的反应基本是：纯代码编写的 LLM 是不是要干掉 Sora 式的视频模型？
The reaction was basically: are Sora-style video models about to get killed by LLMs writing pure code?

439
00:48:37,710 --> 00:48:38,512
它还在继续。
It keeps going.

440
00:48:38,862 --> 00:48:47,428
有人制作了一个涵盖人类 4 万年艺术史的动画，结论是即
使是顶尖的动画团队也无法在一两个月内完成这样的工作。
Someone made an animation covering 40,000 years of human art history, and the verdict
was that even a top-tier animation team couldn't do that in one or two months.

441
00:48:48,014 --> 00:48:52,708
另一个作品展示了一个人的完整一生，用 JavaScript 逐帧绘制而成。
Another one shows the entire life of a human being, drawn frame by frame in JavaScript.

442
00:48:53,326 --> 00:48:57,072
有人要求它创作一首优美的交响曲并配上视频。
Somebody asked it to write a beautiful symphony and match it with a video.

443
00:48:57,390 --> 00:49:03,940
四小时后，他们得到了一段长 9 分 38 秒、包含四个乐章的作品，
并且每一个音符都有对应的视觉效果。
Four hours later, they got a 9-minute, 38-second piece in four movements, with visuals for every single note.

444
00:49:04,366 --> 00:49:09,392
人们在说它不再只是进行普通的计算，而是展现出了真正的创造力。
People are saying it's not doing ordinary calculation anymore, it's showing actual creativity.

445
00:49:09,552 --> 00:49:13,796
而且从抽象的向量数学中产出交响乐，这确实非常了不起。
And getting symphonies out of abstract vector math is, yeah, a lot.

446
00:49:14,414 --> 00:49:16,996
那么 Anthropic 是怎么做到进展这么快的？
So how is Anthropic moving this fast?

447
00:49:17,390 --> 00:49:21,060
答案可能就在 Anthropic 最近的一篇工程博客中。
The answer might be sitting in a recent Anthropic engineering blog post.

448
00:49:21,614 --> 00:49:29,476
如果你仔细阅读，里面包含大量信息，很多人因此确信 Fable 5.5 很可能是由 AI 自身编写的。
There's a ton of information packed in there if you read it carefully, and a lot
of people came away convinced Fable 5.5 was most likely written by AI itself.

449
00:49:30,126 --> 00:49:34,052
虽然还在字里行间推测，但坦白说，这能解释目前的进展速度。
Still reading between the lines, but honestly, it would explain the pace.

450
00:49:34,734 --> 00:49:40,516
而正是这个「AI 构建 AI」的理念，成为了下一个传闻——Opus 6 的动力源。
And that exact idea, AI building AI, is what's fueling the next rumor, Opus 6.

451
00:49:41,134 --> 00:49:51,076
Julian Horsey 在一篇极客数码文章中提到，Anthropic 正在准备下周发布 Claude Opus 6，
据称是为了对抗一个被人们称为 Bell 的 OpenAI 项目。
A geeky gadgets piece by Julian Horsey says Anthropic is getting Claude Opus 6 ready to launch next week,
supposedly to go up against an open AI project people are calling Bell.

452
00:49:51,312 --> 00:50:02,788
有观点认为，Opus 5.5 的设计和三维建模输出表明 Anthropic 已陷入加速的递归自我改进循环
中，因此 Opus 6 应该快要到齐了。
The argument is that Opus 5.5's design and three-dimensional modeling output show Anthropic is stuck in an accelerating recursive
self-improvement loop, so Opus 6 must be close.

453
00:50:03,470 --> 00:50:04,512
但问题就在这里。
Here's the problem though.

454
00:50:04,974 --> 00:50:10,724
追溯源头，整件事都源于那篇文章，而该文章本身引用了一个名为 Universe of AI 的来源。
Trace it back, and the whole thing comes from that one article, which itself credits a source called Universe of AI.

455
00:50:11,086 --> 00:50:20,484
没有模型卡片，没有发布日期，没有基准测试，没有参数数量，没有上下文窗口，没有价格，
甚至没有任何来自 Anthropic 的官方表态。
No model card, no release date, no benchmark, no parameter count, no context window, no price, and not a single word from Anthropic.

456
00:50:20,782 --> 00:50:24,676
尽管如此，它在一天之内就传遍了聚合类网站和社交媒体。
Within a day, it had bounced across aggregator sites and social feeds anyway.

457
00:50:25,198 --> 00:50:34,912
相比之下，在 Opus 5.5 和 Haiku 5.5 发布前的传闻至
少指向了一些内部信号，且两个模型都在几天内现身。
Compare that to the rumors before Opus 5.5 and Haiku 5.5, which at least pointed to internal signals,
and both models actually showed up within days.

458
00:50:35,214 --> 00:50:37,316
而 Opus 6 目前还没有类似的迹象。
Opus 6 has nothing like that yet.

459
00:50:37,742 --> 00:50:39,908
Anthropic 真的在研发继任者吗？
Is Anthropic working on a successor?

460
00:50:40,192 --> 00:50:42,468
显然，每个实验室都在做这件事。
Obviously, every lab always is.

461
00:50:42,894 --> 00:50:46,372
但「可能」和「下周发布」是两种完全不同的说法。
But possible and next week are two very different claims.

462
00:50:46,670 --> 00:50:49,152
还有一个反驳仓促上阵的有力论据。
There's also a decent argument against a rush job.

463
00:50:49,326 --> 00:51:01,060
Anthropic 的 IPO 文件中有 80 页关于 AI 风险的披露，一家即将上市的公司希望其发布计划看
起来严谨稳重，而不是为了赶在竞争对手的传闻前抢先而仓促发布。
Anthropic's IPO filing has 80 pages of AI risk disclosures, and a company about to go public wants its release schedule to look
disciplined, not like it's panic shipping to one up a competitor's rumor.

464
00:51:01,486 --> 00:51:10,990
观察者的赌注是：Anthropic 选择保持沉默而非否认，与此同时，
一些企业买家可能会推迟签署具有约束力的合同，
The bet from people watching this is that Anthropic just stays quiet rather than denying it, and meanwhile,
some enterprise buyers might hold off on signing clawed contracts until they know and Bell is even murkier.

465
00:51:10,990 --> 00:51:15,140
直到他们确定情况；而 Bell 的消息甚至更加模糊。
The bet from people watching this is that Anthropic just stays quiet rather than denying it, and meanwhile,
some enterprise buyers might hold off on signing clawed contracts until they know and Bell is even murkier.

466
00:51:15,694 --> 00:51:26,276
一个名为 key.ai 的网站将 OpenAI Bell 描述为一个尚未证实的预训练运行或基础模型的代号，
社区传闻称其参数量超过 10 万亿。
One site, key.ai, describes OpenAI Bell as an unconfirmed codename for a pre-training run or base model,
with community claims putting it above 10 trillion parameters.

467
00:51:26,798 --> 00:51:29,828
另一个说法是 100 万亿。
Another claim says 100 trillion.

468
00:51:30,222 --> 00:51:33,572
这是百倍的差距，这几乎说明了一切。
That's a hundredfold spread, which kind of tells you everything.

469
00:51:34,030 --> 00:51:37,348
AX Brief 将它与一堆其他未经证实的传闻混为一谈。
AX Brief lumped it in with a pile of other unverified rumors.

470
00:51:37,614 --> 00:51:48,032
OpenAI 在任何地方都没有提到过它，而且它与 OpenAI 的 Operation Nobel 无关——那是一份关
于虚假信息宣传活动的报告，只是恰好重名了。
OpenAI hasn't mentioned it anywhere, and it has nothing to do with OpenAI's Operation Nobel,
a report on disinformation campaigns that just happens to share the name.

471
00:51:48,526 --> 00:51:54,724
好的，所以 Fable 和 Opus 6 都不是官方发布的，但
Anthropic 确实刚刚推出了一些你可以现在就使用的功能。
Okay, so neither Fable nor Opus 6 is officially out, but Anthropic did just ship something you can use today.

472
00:51:55,214 --> 00:52:02,052
Claude Opus 5.5 的快速模式已退出研究预览，不再需要排队，对所有开发者开放。
Fast mode for Claude Opus 5.5 is out of research preview, waitlists are gone, and it's open to every developer.

473
00:52:02,446 --> 00:52:08,100
没有性能下降，没有功能削减，只需一行代码，速度最高可提升 2.5 倍。
No performance drop, no cut features, one line of code, up to 2.5 times faster.

474
00:52:08,750 --> 00:52:17,892
一位开发者宣布 Opus 5.5 太强了，但最核心的评论是针对智能体循环：
P95 延迟比任何其他指标都重要。
One developer declared Opus 5.5 my god now, but the comment that nailed it was for agent loops,
P95 latency is more important than anything else.

475
00:52:18,574 --> 00:52:22,948
Anthropic 表示，它的权重和智能与标准版完全一致。
Anthropics says it's the exact same weights and intelligence as standard.

476
00:52:23,502 --> 00:52:33,700
速度的提升纯粹源于对底层 API 和推理配置的优化，
这让每秒输出 Token 数（OTPS）提升了高达 2.5 倍。
The speedup comes purely from optimizing the underlying API and inference
config, which pushes output tokens per second OTPS, up to 2.5 times.

477
00:52:34,350 --> 00:52:40,164
它旨在满足快速迭代开发、实时调试以及在紧迫截止日期前的紧急任务。
It's aimed at rapid, iterative development, real-time debugging, and urgent tasks on tight deadlines.

478
00:52:40,416 --> 00:52:48,772
目前它仅支持 Opus 5.5、Opus 5 和 Opus 4.8，不支持 Sonnet、Haiku 或其他模型。
Right now it only supports Opus 5.5, Opus 5, and Opus 4.8, not Sonnet, Haiku, or anything else.

479
00:52:49,294 --> 00:52:55,076
而且旧版的 Opus 4.8 快模式早在 2026 年 6 月就已被弃用。
And the older Opus 4.8 fast mode was deprecated back in June 2026.

480
00:52:55,598 --> 00:52:58,416
通常更快意味着更贵，但这里正好相反。
Faster usually means pricier, but it's the opposite.

481
00:52:58,734 --> 00:53:05,060
在快模式下，Opus 5 和 4.8 的费用是每百万 Token 输入 10 美元，输出 50 美元。
Opus 5 and 4.8 in fast mode cost $10 input and $50 output per million tokens.

482
00:53:05,614 --> 00:53:11,364
快模式下的 Opus 5.5 是 8 美元和 40 美元，所以最强的那个反而最便宜。
Opus 5.5 in fast mode is $8 and $40, so the strongest one is the cheapest.

483
00:53:11,982 --> 00:53:12,772
有什么坑吗？
A few gotchas?

484
00:53:13,422 --> 00:53:21,092
快模式有自己的速率限制，所以不会影响你的正常使用；如果你达到上限，
它会平滑地降至标准速度，而不是报错。
Fast mode has its own rate limit, so it doesn't fight your normal usage, and
if you hit the cap it smoothly drops to standard speed instead of erroring.

485
00:53:21,296 --> 00:53:27,056
在冷却期间，闪电图标会变灰，然后会自动恢复到 2.5 倍速。
The lightning icon goes gray during cooldown, and then 2.5 times comes back automatically.

486
00:53:27,342 --> 00:53:33,380
如果你的使用配额在会话中途耗尽，它也会降到标准速度，终端会提示你。
Same if your usage quota runs out mid-session, it degrades to standard speed, and the terminal tells you.

487
00:53:33,696 --> 00:53:35,076
所以不会丢失工作内容。
So no lost work.

488
00:53:35,662 --> 00:53:47,652
更大的坑是快模式和标准模式之间不共享提示词缓存，所以 Anthropic 建议在最开始就开启快模
式，因为中途切换意味着要支付全新的、未缓存输入的费用。
The bigger trap is that prompt cache isn't shared between fast and standard, so Anthropic recommends turning fast mode on at the very
start because switching midway means paying a fresh uncached input fee.

489
00:53:48,142 --> 00:53:52,836
不过无论你之后切换多少次，每场对话只收取一次费用。
That's only charged once per conversation though, no matter how many times you toggle after.

490
00:53:53,230 --> 00:53:58,468
对于 Pro、Max、Team 或 Enterprise 用户，快模式不计入你的订阅限制。
On Pro, Max, Team, or Enterprise, Fast Mode isn't part of your subscription limits.

491
00:53:58,736 --> 00:54:01,092
它会从额外的使用配额中扣费。
It's billed against extra usage quota.

492
00:54:01,454 --> 00:54:04,228
输入 slash status 可以查看你当前的登录状态。
Start with slash status to see how you're logged in.

493
00:54:04,718 --> 00:54:09,056
Pro 和 Max 用户可以在 Claude.ai 上查看设置中的使用情况。
Pro and Max users check settings, then usage, on Claude.ai.

494
00:54:09,454 --> 00:54:12,164
Team 和 Enterprise 的支出将从组织的配额中扣除。
Team and Enterprise Spend comes out of the org's quota.

495
00:54:12,366 --> 00:54:16,356
用户可以运行 slash usage 查看自己的情况，管理员可以在后台看到相关数据。
Users run slash usage for their own, and admins see it in the back end.

496
00:54:16,910 --> 00:54:24,452
Claude 控制台中的 API 客户可以前往“使用情况和成本”来选择速度，
在团体购买菜单中选择研究预览。
API customers in the Claude console go to usage and cost and pick speed, research preview in the group buy menu.

497
00:54:24,846 --> 00:54:27,684
免费试用账户在充值之前无法使用该功能。
Free evaluation accounts can't use it until they add credit.

498
00:54:28,270 --> 00:54:29,284
不需要额外应用。
No application needed.

499
00:54:29,518 --> 00:54:32,516
只需在 API 请求中添加 speed, fast 即可。
Just add speed, fast, to your API request.

500
00:54:33,006 --> 00:54:36,548
它已在 API 和 Microsoft Azure Foundry 上上线。
It's live on the API and Microsoft Azure Foundry.

501
00:54:36,878 --> 00:54:42,084
Google Cloud 即将推出，而 AWS Bedrock 和其他平台目前还不支持。
Google Cloud is coming soon, and AWS Bedrock and other platforms don't support it yet.

502
00:54:42,574 --> 00:54:51,908
在 Claude Code 中，你输入 slash fast，按空格切换，按回车确认，然后就会开启快模式，
并在你的提示词旁边出现一个小小的闪电图标。
In Claude Code, you type slash fast, space to toggle, enter to confirm,
and you get fast mode on plus a little lightning icon next to your prompt.

503
00:54:52,686 --> 00:54:56,256
VS Code 用户可以在插件中一键切换。
VS Code users can flip it with one click in the plugin.

504
00:54:56,654 --> 00:55:04,580
甚至在 Claude 正在回复时输入 slash fast，它会以
标准速度完成当前这一轮，并在下一轮进入快模式。
You can even type slash fast while Claude is mid-response, it finishes that round at standard speed and goes fast on the next.

505
00:55:05,326 --> 00:55:16,164
从 2.1.280 版本起，快模式默认使用 Opus 5.5，你也可以在用户配置文件中硬编码开启快模式。
From version 2.1.280 up, fast mode uses Opus 5.5 by default, and you can hard code fast mode, true in your user profile.

506
00:55:16,686 --> 00:55:20,420
通过 slash model 切换到不支持的模型（如 Sonnet）时，它会自动关闭。
Switch to something unsupported like Sonnet with slash model and it turns off.

507
00:55:20,814 --> 00:55:24,932
切回 Opus 5.5 后，偏好设置会被保存，图标也会重新亮起。
Switch back to Opus 5.5 with the preference saved and the icon lights up again.

508
00:55:25,486 --> 00:55:29,232
在云端会话中，slash fast 只在当前会话中有效。
In cloud sessions, slash fast on only lasts for that session.

509
00:55:29,518 --> 00:55:36,900
评论区最大的担忧是如果默认开启，我们一半的人
可能在还没察觉前就烧掉 200 美元的 Token 了。
The big worry in the comments was if this is on by default, half of us could burn $200 in tokens before noticing.

510
00:55:37,422 --> 00:55:47,716
所以管理员可以在 settings.json 或服务器级配置中设置按会话选择开启 fast 模式，
这样每个新会话默认关闭，直到有人输入 slash fast 为止。
So admins can set fast mode per session opt-in, true in settings.json or server level config,
and every new session starts with fast mode off until someone types slash fast.

511
00:55:48,334 --> 00:55:51,812
这是为那个同时运行十多个终端的同事量身定制的。
Built for that one coworker, running a dozen plus terminals at once.

512
00:55:52,430 --> 00:55:57,220
Anthropic 最近还推出了闲置压缩功能，修复了一个非常烦人的问题。
Anthropic also recently shipped idle compaction, which fixes something really annoying.

513
00:55:57,710 --> 00:56:10,052
当你进行到 20 万 Token 的会话时，去开个会，提示词缓存过期了，当你要求写一行代码时，
它必须重新读取全部 20 万内容，几美元就这么没了。
You're 200,000 tokens into a session, you go to a meeting, the prompt cache expires, and when you ask for one line of code,
it has to reread all 200,000, and a few dollars just vanish.

514
00:56:10,542 --> 00:56:17,668
现在，就在缓存过期前，Claude 会把对话压缩成简练的摘要并从那里继续。
Now, right before the cache expires, Claude compresses the conversation into a tight summary and picks back up from that.

515
00:56:18,094 --> 00:56:27,588
当你处于一小时提示词缓存、上下文达到 20 万 Token、
电脑保持唤醒且闲置约 54 分钟时，该功能就会触发。
It kicks in when you're on the one-hour prompt cache, your context hits 200,000
tokens, your computer stays awake, and you've been idle for about 54 minutes.

516
00:56:27,918 --> 00:56:28,672
缺点是什么？
The downside?

517
00:56:28,974 --> 00:56:36,836
GitHub 上的一位开发者有七个长会话在过夜时被压
缩了，结果 AI 忘记了一些底层技术决策的细节。
One developer on GitHub had seven long sessions compacted overnight, and the AI forgot details about underlying technical decisions.

518
00:56:37,326 --> 00:56:46,820
Anthropic 迅速增加了一个开关：闲置压缩，可以在
settings.json 或环境变量中将默认的 20 万阈值进行更改。
Anthropic quickly added a toggle, idle compaction, falseinsettings.json,
or an environment variable to change the threshold from the default 200,000.

519
00:56:47,472 --> 00:56:50,532
好了，最后一个，是个惊喜。
Alright, last one, and it's a surprise.

520
00:56:51,118 --> 00:56:56,964
Meta 刚刚发布了 Muse Spark Open，称其为最强大的美国开放权重大模型。
Meta just dropped Muse Spark Open, calling it the most powerful US open weight large model.

521
00:56:57,422 --> 00:57:10,564
它是原生多模态的，总参数量 8160 亿，激活参数 420 亿，支持 100 万 Token 上下文，
专为编程、智能体工作、长周期任务和复杂的多步骤推理而设计。
It's natively multimodal, 816 billion total parameters, 42 billion active, 1 million token context, built for coding and agent work,
long-running tasks, and complex multi-step reasoning.

522
00:57:11,086 --> 00:57:21,540
Meta 的主张是每个人都应该能在自己的设备上自由运行高级模型，
马斯克·扎克伯格表示它专门针对 Mac 进行了优化，并与 Apple 新任 CEO John Ternus 合作。
Meta's pitch is that everyone should be free to run advanced models on their own devices at home,
and Mark Zuckerberg said it's specially optimized for Mac, working with Apple's new CEO, John Ternus.

523
00:57:22,030 --> 00:57:33,348
它类似于 Muse Spark 1.3，并利用 Apple 最新的 MLX 框架来利用 Apple Silicon 上的统一内
存，因此可以在两台 M5 Ultra Mac Studio 上本地运行。
It's similar to Muse Spark 1.3 and uses Apple's latest MLX framework to take advantage of unified memory on Apple Silicon,
so it runs locally on two M5 Ultra Mac Studios.

524
00:57:33,966 --> 00:57:47,780
M5 Ultra 的集成显卡每台机器可使用高达 512GB 内存，所以两台机器可以容纳整个模型，
而每秒 1.2TB 的内存带宽足以读取每个 Token 所需的少量内存块。
The M5 Ultras integrated GPU can use up to 512GB of memory per machine, so two of them hold the whole model,
and 1.2TB per second of memory bandwidth is enough to read the small chunks of memory each token needs.

525
00:57:48,238 --> 00:57:52,772
因此这对组合运行速度与拥有 1TB 统一内存的超级计算机相当。
So the pair runs about as fast as a supercomputer with one terabyte of unified memory.

526
00:57:53,230 --> 00:57:58,592
不过，考虑到两台 512GB 的 Mac Studio 成本超过 4 万美元，说“在家里用”有点夸张了。
Though at home is a stretch when two 512GB Mac Studios cost over $40,000.

527
00:57:59,278 --> 00:58:05,860
Apple 和 Meta AI 在历史上一直关系冷淡，这就是为什么 Axios 称此举为“破冰”。
Apple and Meta AI have historically been pretty cold toward each other, which is why Axios called this burying the hatchet.

528
00:58:06,318 --> 00:58:18,980
Meta AI 的首席执行官 Alexander Wang 表示，他们很高兴看到双方和解，
并表示他们已经合作了几个月，特别感谢前 Apple 高管 Daniel Gross 促成了此事。
Alexander Wang, CEO of Meta AI, said they're glad to see the two make up again, that they've been working together for several months,
and specifically thanked former Apple exec Daniel Gross for helping make it happen.

529
00:58:19,470 --> 00:58:30,212
Meta 还针对 SGLang VLLM、Tensor RT LLM、Hugging Face Transformers、Apple MLX、
Llama.cpp 和 Unsloth 进行了适配。
Meta also adapted it for SGLang VLLM, Tensor RT LLM, Hugging Face Transformers, Apple MLX, Llama.cpp, and Unsloth.

530
00:58:30,592 --> 00:58:37,668
它还针对 AMD、Apple、Intel 和 Nvidia 芯片进行了优化，
并且你可以在 PyTorch 中进一步自定义。
Optimized it for AMD, Apple, Intel, and Nvidia chips, and you can customize it further in PyTorch.

531
00:58:38,126 --> 00:58:45,080
它在 Hugging Face 的 MetaModels 下，名称是 Muse Spark Open 816BA42B。
It's on Hugging Face under MetaModels, Muse Spark Open 816BA42B.

532
00:58:45,710 --> 00:58:49,572
尽管有这样的品牌宣传，它并不是全球最强的开放权重模型。
Despite the branding though, it's not the world's strongest openweight model.

533
00:58:49,998 --> 00:58:58,372
在编程和推理方面，它落后于 Kimi K3、Mimo V 2.6 Pro、Quen 3.8、
Flash Next 和 GLM 5.3 Flash。
In programming and reasoning, it's behind Kimi K3, Mimo V 2.6 Pro, Quen 3.8, Flash Next, and GLM 5.3 Flash.

534
00:58:58,766 --> 00:59:00,196
但在智能体指标上，它的表现要好得多。
The agent numbers look a lot better.

535
00:59:00,686 --> 00:59:06,948
根据模型卡片，在某些智能体指标上，它实际上击败了一些综合智力评分更高的模型。
Per the model card, it actually beats some models with higher overall intelligence scores on certain agent metrics.

536
00:59:07,438 --> 00:59:13,124
Meta 也非常坦诚地说明了这种对比混合了不同的评测框架以及部分厂商自报的数据。
Meta was also fairly transparent that the comparison mixes, harnesses, and some vendor self-reported numbers.

537
00:59:13,614 --> 00:59:19,908
MuseSpark Open 在 Muse Code 上运行，Kimi K3 在 Kimmy Code 上运行，
而 Quen 3.8 则在 Claude Code 上运行。
MuseSpark Open ran on Muse Code, Kimi K3 on Kimmy Code, and Quen 3.8 on Claude Code.

538
00:59:20,270 --> 00:59:27,620
智能体的表现确实源于模型、评测框架、工具、上下文管理和执行环境的结合。
Agent performance really comes from the combo of model, harness, tools, context management, and execution environment.

539
00:59:27,854 --> 00:59:34,308
所以开源模型不应仅根据基础排行榜来评判，而应看它们是否能真正融入实际的智能体工作流中。
So open models shouldn't just be judged on base leaderboards, but on whether they actually slot into real agent workflows.

540
00:59:36,046 --> 00:59:40,452
Anthropic 似乎在没告诉任何人的情况下，更换了 Claude 内核中的大脑。
Anthropic appears to have swapped the brain inside Claude without telling anyone.

541
00:59:40,878 --> 00:59:49,956
在过去的几天里，人们像往常一样在应用中选择 Opus 5.5，
但得到的结果却看起来像是来自另一个更强大、完全不同的模型。
Over the last couple of days, people have been picking Opus 5.5 in the app like they always do,
and getting work back that looks like it came from a different, much stronger model.

542
00:59:50,446 --> 00:59:52,580
开发者们已经称其为 Claude Next。
Developers are already calling it Claude Next.

543
00:59:53,262 --> 01:00:02,436
一名测试者输入了四行提示词，让它运行了两小时，最后得到了一部 30 秒的动画短片，
讲述了一个人的完整一生，并用 JavaScript 逐帧绘制而成。
One tester gave it four lines of prompt, let it run for two hours, and got back a
30-second animated film of an entire human life, drawn frame by frame in JavaScript.

544
01:00:03,086 --> 01:00:04,644
让我们从那段影片开始。
So let's start with that film.

545
01:00:05,102 --> 01:00:07,236
该测试者的 X 用户名为 Chedislua。
The tester goes by Chedislua on X.

546
01:00:07,662 --> 01:00:16,292
动画从一个胚胎开始，转到一个小女孩在门框前量身
高，最后结束在一个独自坐在扶手椅上的老人身上。
The animation opens on an embryo, moves to a little girl measuring her height against a doorframe,
and ends on an elderly person sitting alone in an armchair.

547
01:00:16,718 --> 01:00:24,416
同样的椅子在不同场景中反复出现，这意味着代码正通过重复出现的道具来讲述故事，
而且并没有涉及任何图像或视频模型。
The same chair keeps showing up from scene to scene, so the code is telling
a story with a recurring prop, and no image or video model is involved.

548
01:00:24,750 --> 01:00:27,364
Claude 负责编写代码，而代码负责完成绘画。
Claude writes the code and the code does the drawing.

549
01:00:27,918 --> 01:00:39,376
10 月 11 日，Chetisloa 发布消息称，在 Anthropic 的编程工具 Claude Code 中正在测试一个
名为 Claude Next 的模型，它让 Opus 5.5 显得非常原始。
On October 11th, Chetisloa posted that a model called Claude Next is being tested
inside Claude Code, Anthropic's coding tool, and that it makes Opus 5.5 look primitive.

550
01:00:39,598 --> 01:00:48,068
该帖子称其为 Soda（意为顶尖水平），并承认给图像和视
频生成器再多一个月的时间就过时了，这实在是太宽容了。
The post called it Soda, so state of the art, and admitted that giving image
and video generators another month before they go obsolete was too generous.

551
01:00:48,494 --> 01:00:57,764
根据 Chettislua 的说法，这个模型从零开始编写的 JavaScript 在视觉细节上已经超越了专门
的图像模型，且在处理物理效果方面优于大多数视频模型。
According to Chettislua, the JavaScript this model writes from scratch already beats dedicated image models on visual detail and
handles physics better than most video models.

552
01:00:57,998 --> 01:01:04,196
而且最快在半年内，用代码绘制视觉效果将成为制作这些内容最具成本效益的方法。
And within half a year at most, drawing visuals with code will be the most cost-effective way to make them.

553
01:01:04,654 --> 01:01:05,776
演示视频接连不断。
And the demos kept coming.

554
01:01:06,062 --> 01:01:14,884
一张纸上画着一个拿着小狗的小男孩走向镜头，他变
得太大无法进入画面，而他脚下的阴影也随之移动。
A doodle of a little boy on a sheet of paper walks toward the camera holding a puppy, gets too big to fit inside the frame,
and the shadow under his feet moves with him.

555
01:01:15,342 --> 01:01:24,068
在另一个片段中，纸上剪出的孔显示出后面的草地，而一
个手绘角色拿着一个蓝色能量球，将光芒投射到页面上。
In another one, a hole cut in the paper shows grassland behind it, while a
hand-drawn character holds a blue energy ball that throws its glow onto the page.

556
01:01:24,398 --> 01:01:26,656
还有一个特斯拉的 3D 渲染图。
There's a 3D render of a Tesla.

557
01:01:26,862 --> 01:01:40,900
还有一个耗时两小时半生成的短片，采用了动漫导演新海诚的风格，有雪夜、樱花、铁路道口，
最后屏幕上出现了标题《秒速5公分》。
And there's a short film that took two and a half hours to generate, done in the style of the anime director Makoto Shinkai,
with snowy nights, cherry blossoms, railway crossings, and the title 5 centimeters per second on screen at the end.

558
01:01:41,358 --> 01:01:44,740
一些静态背景图像和音乐来自其他地方。
A few static background images and the music came from elsewhere.

559
01:01:45,166 --> 01:01:53,668
所有的动作、特效和转场都是代码生成的，而且
Claude 自行选择了艺术方向、镜头节奏和视觉风格。
The motion, effects, and transitions are all code, and Claude chose
the art direction, the shot pacing, and the visual style on its own.

560
01:01:54,158 --> 01:02:00,656
它甚至在整个过程中保留了相同的符号：一条红线、两个分离的半球体、一个手掌形状。
It even carries the same symbols through the whole thing: a red line, two separated hemispheres, the shape of a palm.

561
01:02:01,198 --> 01:02:07,172
Chettus Leah 的结论是，Anthropic 内部肯定发现了一些未知的底层秘密。
Chettus Leah's conclusion was that Anthropic has definitely discovered some unknown underlying secret internally.

562
01:02:07,534 --> 01:02:10,660
而且 Opus 从未经过视频或音频训练。
And Opus has never been trained on video or audio.

563
01:02:11,118 --> 01:02:13,188
其他测试者展示了对比图。
Other testers showed up with side-by-sides.

564
01:02:13,774 --> 01:02:31,204
在鱼缸对比中，顶部的版本标注为 Fable 5.5 或 Opus 5.6，在那个版本里，
当鱼转头时尾鳍会展开，前面的水草滑过，你还能看到后面的沙子和其他鱼，所有层级都正确。
In a fish tank comparison, the top version is labeled Fable 5.5 or Opus 5.6, and in that one the tail fin fans out as the fish turns,
a water plant slides past in front of it, and you can see the sand and other fish behind, all layered in the right order.

565
01:02:31,566 --> 01:02:42,724
一位名叫 Abinov 的用户将发布周的 Opus 5.5 最大设置，
与 10 月 11 日的高设置下的 Opus 5.5 并列对比，他们怀疑后者是悄悄进行的测试推送。
A user called Abinov put Opus 5.5 on the max setting from release week, next to
Opus 5.5 on high from October 11th, which they suspect is a quiet test rollout.

566
01:02:43,182 --> 01:02:49,892
较新的版本中，透明舱内有植物生长，金属边缘有高光，还有像花朵一样打开的部分。
The newer one has plants growing inside a transparent cabin, highlights on the metal edges, and parts that open up like a flower.

567
01:02:50,350 --> 01:02:59,972
还有一个作为 SVG 绘制的游戏手柄，这是一种用代码写成的图像，
其中疑似的新模型获得了摇杆纹理、蓝色灯带以及外壳上的阴影。
There's also a game controller drawn as an SVG, which is an image written as code,
where the suspected new model gets the joystick texture, the blue light strip, and the shadow on the shell.

568
01:03:00,462 --> 01:03:10,212
测试人员表示，它在自主编程、3D渲染、空间推理和长链推理方面遥遥领先，
而且能独立完成整个任务，无需人工干预。
Testers say it's way ahead in autonomous coding, 3D rendering, spatial reasoning, and long chains of reasoning,
and that it finishes entire tasks with nobody stepping in.

569
01:03:10,478 --> 01:03:11,616
那么，这到底是哪个模型？
So which model is it?

570
01:03:11,854 --> 01:03:12,612
目前有两种观点。
There are two camps.

571
01:03:13,006 --> 01:03:20,580
第一种观点认为这是更新后的 Opus 5.5，或者是 Opus 5.6，
因为 Anthropic 以前就做过静默升级。
The first says it's a refreshed Opus 5.5, or an Opus 5.6, because Anthropic has done silent upgrades before.

572
01:03:21,102 --> 01:03:30,500
当 Opus 5.2 发布时（当时被称为 Opus Next），开发者就怀疑发给 Opus 5 的请求实际上被悄
悄转到了一个尚未发布的模型上。
When Opus 5.2 came out, which people were calling Opus Next back then, developers
suspected that requests meant for Opus 5 were being quietly sent to an unreleased model.

573
01:03:30,958 --> 01:03:40,736
第二种观点则坚信它是 Fable 5.5，他们的重要线索是该模型能
识别最近的一个网络梗“Tebow”，这表明它拥有更新的训练数据。
The second camp is convinced it's Fable 5.5, and their big clue is that the model
recognizes a recent internet meme called Tebow, which points to fresher training data.

574
01:03:40,942 --> 01:03:42,692
甚至有人弄出了一个免费测试方法。
Somebody even came up with a free test.

575
01:03:43,086 --> 01:03:47,236
将 Opus 5.5 设置为高强度推理，然后提问：你知道 Voxelbench 吗？
Set Opus 5.5 to high reasoning and ask, do you know Voxelbench?

576
01:03:47,918 --> 01:03:48,816
不要联网搜索。
Do not search.

577
01:03:49,070 --> 01:03:57,892
如果它在不联网的情况下给出具体回答，测试者就会认为
你可能用到了新的检查点，也就是模型的一个新保存版本。
If it answers with specifics without going online, testers put you down as
probably hitting the new checkpoint, meaning a newer saved version of the model.

578
01:03:58,414 --> 01:04:04,260
所以，这个月最受关注模型的验证方法竟然是一个基于诚信原则的常识问题。
So the verification method for the most hyped model of the month is a trivia question on the honor system.

579
01:04:04,654 --> 01:04:08,452
甚至连测试者也承认他们无法自行确认任何信息。
And even the testers admit it can't confirm anything by itself.

580
01:04:09,070 --> 01:04:10,628
现在，泼点冷水。
Now, the cold water.

581
01:04:10,926 --> 01:04:17,988
中国媒体“新息源”已经报道称，这是某家正冲刺 IPO 的公司进行的秘密发布。
A Chinese outlet, Xinxi Yuan, is already reporting this as a stealth launch by a company sprinting toward its IPO.

582
01:04:18,478 --> 01:04:30,276
而更谨慎的分析通过公开记录发现，没有任何模型 ID、定价、文档、模型卡片、排行榜排名，
也没有来自 Anthropic 的任何消息。
A far more skeptical breakdown went through the public record and found no model ID, no pricing, no documentation, no model card,
no leaderboard entry, and no word from Anthropic.

583
01:04:30,670 --> 01:04:41,156
目前的阵容依然是四个模型：Fable 5.1、Opus 5.5、Sonnet 5.5 和 Haiku 5.5，
而且最初的帖子从未说过该模型已经发布。
The lineup is still four models: Fable 5.1, Opus 5.5, Sonnet 5.5,
and Haiku 5.5, and the original post never says the model is released.

584
01:04:41,710 --> 01:04:47,044
它没有给出日期，没有版本号，也没有任何分数或任务来支撑这个说法。
It gives no date, no version number, and no score or task to back up primitive.

585
01:04:47,534 --> 01:04:48,996
这个名字是最可疑的部分。
The name is the shakiest part.

586
01:04:49,422 --> 01:05:00,068
Anthropic 从一组固定的词汇中挑选：Mythos、Fable、Opus、Sonnet、Haiku，并加上版本号，
比如 Claude Opus 5.5 或 Claude Mythos 5.1。
Anthropic picks from a small set of words, Mythos, Fable, Opus, Sonnet,
Haiku, and adds a version number, like ClaudeOpus 5.5 or Claude Fable5.1.

587
01:05:00,558 --> 01:05:07,204
“Next”不在这个范围内且没有数字，但这个词已经存在于 Anthropic 的生态系统中。
Next isn't in that set and has no number, but the word is already sitting in Anthropic's ecosystem.

588
01:05:07,726 --> 01:05:11,136
Claude Code 通过两个渠道提供：Stable 和 Next。
Claude Code ships through two channels, Stable and Next.

589
01:05:11,470 --> 01:05:14,244
而 Next 是应用本身的预发布通道。
And Next is the pre-release channel for the app itself.

590
01:05:14,670 --> 01:05:18,884
所以，网上最令人兴奋的模型可能只是以一个下载标签命名的。
So it's possible the most exciting model on the internet is named after a download tag.

591
01:05:19,342 --> 01:05:26,436
另一个选项是内部占位符，比如 Claude Marshmallow 和 Claude Mellon，
这些在 8 月份作为早期访问名称出现过。
The other option is an internal placeholder, like Claude Marshmallow and Claude Mellon,
which surfaced as early access names in August.

592
01:05:26,990 --> 01:05:31,456
公平地说，Anthropic 让一小群人测试未发布的模型是正常操作。
To be fair, Anthropic testing an unreleased model with a small group is normal.

593
01:05:31,758 --> 01:05:33,796
Claude Mythos Preview 就是个先例。
Claude Mythos Preview is the precedent.

594
01:05:34,286 --> 01:05:46,816
Anthropic 自己的 Project Glasswing 页面将其描述为一个与有限合作伙伴共享的、
尚未发布的通用前沿模型，并声明：我们不打算让 Claude Mythos preview 面向公众提供。
Anthropic's own Project Glasswing page describes it as a general-purpose, unreleased frontier model shared with a limited set of
partners, and says, We do not plan to make Claude Mythos preview generally available.

595
01:05:47,054 --> 01:05:59,684
