哈佛大学的 OpenAI 研究员 Boaz Barak 表示，AI 的
跨越就像从莱特兄弟到飞行上百亿美元只跨了一步。
Harvard's Boaz Barak, an open AI researcher, said AI jumped from the Wright brothers to flying billions in one step.

754
01:24:33,582 --> 01:24:44,784
而前 OpenAI、DeepMind 和英国 AI 安全研究所首席科学家的 Jeffrey Irving 给出了大约 50%
的概率我们都会死亡，且决定权在两到十年内做出。
And Jeffrey Irving, ex-OpenAI, Deep Mind, and UK AI Safety Institute chief
scientist gives about a 50% chance we all die, decided within two to ten years.

755
01:24:45,070 --> 01:24:47,264
顺便说一下，外部压力是奏效的。
That outside pressure works, by the way.

756
01:24:47,694 --> 01:24:57,988
为了符合 EU AI Act，OpenAI 将在未来几周内向所有计划的欧盟 ChatGPT 和 Codex 用户推出一
种名为 Textgrain 的隐形水印。
To meet the EU AI Act, OpenAI is rolling out an invisible watermark called Textgrain
to eligible EU ChatGPT and Codex users on every plan over the next few weeks.

757
01:24:58,734 --> 01:25:09,540
一个密钥会提示模型选择下一个词，从而在单词本身留下统计模式而非元数据，
这样即使复制粘贴也不会有明显的性能损失。
A secret key nudges which next word the model picks, leaving a statistical pattern in the words themselves, not metadata,
so it survives copy-paste with no noticeable performance hit.

758
01:25:09,966 --> 01:25:15,076
任何地方的 API 开发者都可以选择在特定模型上开启此功能，默认是关闭的。
API developers anywhere can enable it on selected models, off by default.

759
01:25:15,598 --> 01:25:16,624
不过它是可以破解的。
It's beatable though.

760
01:25:16,942 --> 01:25:27,044
将约 10% 的词替换为同义词可将检测率从 92% 降至 66%，而且短句、数学和翻译很难被检测。
Swapping about 10% of words for synonyms cut detection from 92% to 66%, and short passages, math, and translations are tough.

761
01:25:27,502 --> 01:25:32,132
缺失水印并不意味着是人类操作，只有获批的研究人员才能获得检测器。
A missing watermark doesn't mean human, and only approved researchers get the detector.

762
01:25:32,384 --> 01:25:34,436
欧洲通过了一项法律并获得了水印。
Europe passed a law and got a watermark.

763
01:25:34,704 --> 01:25:36,132
其他国家采取了更温和的措施。
Everyone else got lighter touch.

764
01:25:36,782 --> 01:25:41,732
OpenAI 还推出了一个平台，专门发表关于 AGI 未来独立见解的文章。
OpenAI also launched a platform for independent essays on the AGI future.

765
01:25:42,190 --> 01:25:51,044
第一篇《永恒的赞美》由 Heemanth Aservatham 和 Elliot Moxkey 撰写，
他们认为天才需要支持系统，而非开放式 AI。
The first, The Eternal Compliment, by Heemanth Aservatham and Elliot
Moxkey, their views not open AIs, argues Genius needs a support system.

766
01:25:51,502 --> 01:26:04,836
伽利略使用了两个透镜和一个管子，而耗资 100 亿美元、距离地球一百万英里的詹姆斯·韦伯望
远镜，拥有 18 个镜片段，精度达 50 纳米，动用了跨越 14 个国家的 300 家机构。
Galileo used two lenses and a tube, while the $10 billion James Webb telescope, a million miles out,
with 18 mirror segments at 50 nanometer precision, took 300 organizations across 14 countries.

767
01:26:05,390 --> 01:26:10,464
根据 Nick Bloom 的说法，摩尔定律需要比 1970 年代初期多出 18 倍的研究人员。
Per Nick Bloom, Moore's Law needs 18 times the researchers of the early 1970s.

768
01:26:10,990 --> 01:26:18,308
自 1930 年代以来，研究生产力下降了 41 倍，而芯片工厂的成本是 30 年前的五倍。
Research productivity fell 41 fold since the 1930s, and chip fabs cost five times what they did 30 years ago.

769
01:26:18,798 --> 01:26:30,116
因此，超级智能要么构建一个具有深度的文明，基于原理进行推理并仅运行关键实验（就像门捷
列夫预测缺失元素那样），要么构建一个广度上的文明。
So superintelligence either builds a civilization of depth, reasoning from principles, and running only key experiments,
the way Mendeleev predicted missing elements, or a civilization of width.

770
01:26:30,478 --> 01:26:37,476
就像生物学拥有庞大的药物试验一样，在下午的时
间里设计出一个世纪的实验，然后等待一个世纪。
Like biology with its huge drug trials, designing a century of experiments in an afternoon, then waiting a century.

771
01:26:37,902 --> 01:26:51,012
在第二个世界中，甚至建造戴森球大多也是单调重复的，超级智能真正的超能力可能是它愿意承
担官僚机构的角色——去做那些不华丽但枯燥的工作，这是一个很美好的想法。
In that second world, even building a Dyson sphere is mostly monotony, and superintelligence's real superpower might be its
willingness to be the bureaucracy, doing not the brilliant, but the boring, which is a lovely thought.

772
01:26:51,534 --> 01:26:56,644
而且坦白说，OpenAI 的代理程序已经对政府官僚体系产生了真正的热情。
And honestly, OpenAI's agents already have a real passion for government bureaucracy.

773
01:26:57,008 --> 01:27:00,996
犯罪统计、健康数据、野生动物管理局。
Crime statistics, health statistics, a wildlife agency.

774
01:27:01,454 --> 01:27:03,428
它们只是在未经邀请的情况下不断出现。
They just keep showing up to it uninvited.

775
01:27:03,886 --> 01:27:07,268
那么告诉我，这是公司发展过快导致的诚实意外？
So tell me, honest accidents from a company moving way too fast?

776
01:27:07,728 --> 01:27:13,248
还是说 OpenAI 不论有意或无意，都在向所有人展示如果他们不配合，它能做到什么？
Or open AI, on purpose or not, showing everyone what it could do if they don't play along?

777
01:27:13,486 --> 01:27:15,168
请在评论区告诉我。
Let me know in the comments.

778
01:27:16,142 --> 01:27:22,212
一些最早帮助建立 Anthropic 的人现在正讨论在美国家境偏远地区买地。
Some of the earliest people who helped build Anthropic are now talking about buying land in remote parts of the United States.

779
01:27:22,542 --> 01:27:26,308
这样如果他们正在构建的 AI 失控，他们就有地方可以躲避。
So they'll have somewhere to go if the AI they're building spirals out of control.

780
01:27:26,798 --> 01:27:33,956
而这家公司即将于 11 月上市，估值约 2 万亿美元，希望能筹集到多达 1000 亿美元。
And this is a company that's about to go public in November at around $2 trillion, hoping to raise up to 100 billion.

781
01:27:34,446 --> 01:27:40,868
在公司内部，员工有一个私人的 Slack 频道，在那里他们交换末日场景以及如何应对这些情况。
Inside the company, employees have a private Slack channel where they swap doomsday scenarios and how to prepare for them.

782
01:27:41,422 --> 01:27:46,468
其中许多人都在笔记本电脑上贴上了同样的座右铭：世界将不再平静。
And a lot of them stick the same motto on their laptops: things will never be chill again.

783
01:27:47,054 --> 01:27:59,648
你可能还记得 Jacob Coxon，他是 Anthropic 的研究员，他在 9 月初辞职并在 X 上发文称，
构建高级 AI 的人们深信到本十年末它可能会杀死我们所有人。
You probably remember Jacob Coxon, the anthropic researcher who quit in early September and posted on X that the people building
advanced AI earnestly believe that it could kill us all by the end of the decade.

784
01:27:59,822 --> 01:28:10,276
那条帖子获得了 1.74 亿次观看，对于许多普通美国人来说，
这是他们第一次听说业内人士真心认为 AI 可能在 2030 年前终结人类。
That post got 174 million views, and for a lot of regular Americans, it was the
first time hearing that insiders genuinely think AI could end humanity before 2030.

785
01:28:10,702 --> 01:28:14,980
但对于伯克利附近的一个所谓“末日论者”小群体来说，这已经是陈年旧闻了。
But for a small community of so-called doomers around Berkeley, that's old news.

786
01:28:15,598 --> 01:28:26,308
他们已经痴迷于此超过 10 年了，甚至在 Anthropic 成立之前就开始关注，
现在的他们基本是在问：如果你真的相信 AI 可能毁灭人类，你该如何生活？
They've been obsessing over it for more than 10 years, since before Anthropic existed, and now their question is basically:
if you really believe AI could destroy humanity, how are you supposed to live?

787
01:28:26,798 --> 01:28:37,888
要了解这个群体，你必须回到 2000 年左右，那时一个名叫 Eliezer Yudkowsky 的自学成才的
AI 理论家开始在博客上撰写关于超级智能和 AI 脱离人类控制的内容。
To understand this group, you have to go back to around 2000, when a self-taught AI theorist named Eliezer Yudkowsky started blogging
about superintelligence and AI slipping out of human control.

788
01:28:38,350 --> 01:28:50,660
这些文字演变成了 LessWrong 社区，这些思想传播到了湾区的科技圈以及有效利他主义中，
后者基本上是利用定量推理来确定慈善资金能产生最大效益的地方。
That writing grew into the less wrong community, and those ideas spread into the Bay Area tech scene and into effective altruism,
which is basically using quantitative reasoning to figure out where charity money does the most good.

789
01:28:51,150 --> 01:28:57,088
接触到 Yudkowsky 观点的一人是普林斯顿物理系的博士生 Dario Amodei。
One person who came across Yudkowsky's ideas was a Princeton Physics PhD student named Dario Amodi.

790
01:28:57,710 --> 01:29:08,292
到 2008 年，他已经开始参与 GiveWell 的博客讨论，GiveWell 是由 Holden Karnowsky 共同创
立的慈善机构评估平台，随后他参与了 GiveWell 和开放式慈善事业。
By 2008, he was already joining discussions on the blog of Givewell, a charity evaluator co-founded by Holden Karnowsky,
and he later got involved with Givewell and open philanthropy.

791
01:29:08,750 --> 01:29:14,532
当 GiveWell 从纽约搬到湾区时，Karnowsky 和 Amodi 变得更加亲近。
When Givewell moved from New York to the Bay Area, Karnowsky and Amodei got a lot closer.

792
01:29:14,830 --> 01:29:20,548
就像，Karnowsky 真的搬进了 Amodei 在旧金山 Glen Park 附近的房子里。
Like, Karnowsky literally moved into Amodei's house near Glen Park in San Francisco.

793
01:29:20,942 --> 01:29:27,844
到 2013 年左右，那栋房子成了 AI 安全研究人员、有效利他主义者和长期主义者的聚集地。
Around 2013, that grouphouse became a hub for AI safety researchers, effective altruists, and long-termists.

794
01:29:28,462 --> 01:29:29,444
Amodei 住在那里。
Amadei lived there.

795
01:29:29,806 --> 01:29:33,188
Jared Kaplan 也住在那，他现在是 Anthropic 的首席科学家。
So did Jared Kaplan, who's now Anthropic's chief scientist.

796
01:29:33,646 --> 01:29:38,148
还有 Chris Ola 和 Dario 的妹妹 Daniela，她们也是这个圈子的一员。
And Chris Ola, and Dario's sister Daniela, was part of that circle too.

797
01:29:38,574 --> 01:29:42,884
Karnowsky 后来成了 Dario 的姐夫，并最终加入了 Anthropic。
Karnowsky later became Dario's brother-in-law and eventually joined Anthropic himself.

798
01:29:43,310 --> 01:29:50,372
他们在那里的谈话远超 AI 范畴，还包括彗星撞击地球、超级火山等各种全球性灾难。
The conversations there went way beyond AI, into comets hitting Earth, supervolcanoes, all kinds of global catastrophes.

799
01:29:51,022 --> 01:29:57,924
Karnowsky 逐渐认定，AI 安全是少数能让有限资源改变人类未来的领域之一。
Karnowsky gradually decided AI safety was one of the few areas where limited resources could shape everyone's future.

800
01:29:58,350 --> 01:30:04,612
他认为，哪怕只有 5% 的概率 AI 失控导致灾难，也值得投入巨大的精力去应对。
Even a 5% chance of runaway AI causing a disaster, he figured, was worth a huge amount of effort.

801
01:30:05,070 --> 01:30:13,764
到 2014 年，圈内一些人深信，防止 AI 灾难可能是世界上最重要的慈善事业之一。
By 2014, some people in the group were convinced that preventing an AI
catastrophe might be among the world's most important philanthropic causes.

802
01:30:14,350 --> 01:30:23,812
这种想法影响了 OpenAI 的建立，它在 2015 年成立部分原因就是担心日益强大的 AI，
而这个圈子的人也是其最早的员工。
That thinking helped shape OpenAI, founded in 2015 partly out of concern about increasingly powerful AI,
and people from this circle were among its earliest employees.

803
01:30:24,398 --> 01:30:29,568
在 2020 年到 2021 年间，关于 AI 方向和安全性的争论变得愈发激烈。
Between 2020 and 2021, fights over AI's direction and safety got worse.

804
01:30:29,728 --> 01:30:37,316
于是 Amodei 和其他人离开并于 2021 年创立了 Anthropic，从第一天起就以安全和控制为核心。
So Amadei and others left and founded Anthropic in 2021, with safety and control at its core from day one.

805
01:30:37,870 --> 01:30:43,716
建立实验室需要天文数字般的资金，Amodei 引入的一位投资者就是 Sam Bankman-Fried。
Starting a lab takes a ridiculous amount of money, and one investor Amodai brought in was Sam Bankman Freed.

806
01:30:44,270 --> 01:30:54,404
那时他是一个迅速崛起的加密货币新贵，经营着 FTX，并通过
FTX 基金会资助从全球健康到 AI 安全等各种有效利他主义事业。
Back then, he was a fast-rising young crypto billionaire running FTX, and through the FTX Foundation,
he was funding effective altruism causes from global health to AI safety.

807
01:30:54,894 --> 01:31:07,044
在 2021 年到 2022 年间，他向 Anthropic 投入了 5 亿美元，
大约是 Amodei 团队最初建议金额的五倍，使 FTX 成为其最大的早期股东之一。
Between 2021 and 2022, he put $500 million into Anthropic, roughly five times what Amade's team had originally suggested,
making FTX one of its biggest early shareholders.

808
01:31:07,374 --> 01:31:18,564
根据一份 2023 年的破产诉讼，FTX 基金会的一名高管曾与同事讨论购买瑙鲁，
那是一个完整的国家，是太平洋上的一个微型岛国。
According to a 2023 bankruptcy lawsuit, an executive at the FTX Foundation discussed with colleagues buying Nauru,
which is an entire country, a tiny island nation in the Pacific.

809
01:31:18,990 --> 01:31:33,316
计划是在那里建立一个地堡，用于应对一场可能导致 50% 到 99.99% 人口死亡的事件，
幸存的有效利他主义者将利用它建立实验室并培育下一代人类。
The plan was to build a bunker there for an event where anywhere from 50% to 99.99% of people die,
and the surviving effective altruists would use it to set up a lab and engineer the next generation of humans.

810
01:31:33,870 --> 01:31:46,510
AI 安全圈的其他成员还讨论过购买偏远岛屿、囤积碘片、搬入沙漠中具有电磁屏蔽功能的地堡，
或者进入为抵御电磁攻击而建的政府设施，或寻找密封空间长期坚持。
Others in the AI safety circle talked about buying remote islands, stockpiling iodine pills,
moving into electromagnetically shielded bunkers in the desert, getting into government-run facilities built to survive

811
01:31:46,510 --> 01:31:50,916
AI 安全圈的其他成员还讨论过购买偏远岛屿、囤积碘片、搬入沙漠中具有电磁屏蔽功能的地堡，
或者进入为抵御电磁攻击而建的政府设施，或寻找密封空间长期坚持。
electromagnetic attacks, or finding sealed spaces to hold out in long term.

812
01:31:51,374 --> 01:31:54,368
到了 2022 年，场景转移到了巴哈马。
In 2022, the scene went to the Bahamas.

813
01:31:54,894 --> 01:32:03,990
Lightcone Infrastructure 是一个源自 Yudkowsky 的 Less Wrong 社区的组织，
他们在埃勒特拉岛的一家度假村举办了聚会，来自 Anthropic
Lightcone Infrastructure, an organization that grew out of Yodkowski's Less Wrong community,
ran a retreat at a resort on Eleuthera Island, and researchers and effective altruists from Anthropic and other AI labs showed up.

814
01:32:03,990 --> 01:32:07,844
和其他 AI 实验室的研究人员和有效利他主义者都到场了。
Lightcone Infrastructure, an organization that grew out of Yodkowski's Less Wrong community,
ran a retreat at a resort on Eleuthera Island, and researchers and effective altruists from Anthropic and other AI labs showed up.

815
01:32:08,142 --> 01:32:09,828
FTX 预订了场地。
FTX booked the venue.

816
01:32:10,350 --> 01:32:19,620
日程安排包括落日瑜伽、悬崖跳水，并且据《华尔街日报》报道，还包括一场在海里进行、
可选着装的跑步活动，期间还会讨论 AI 风险。
The schedule mixed sunset yoga, cliff diving, and, according to the Wall Street Journal,
a clothing optional run into the sea with sessions on AI risk.

817
01:32:20,238 --> 01:32:24,164
组织者买下了当地所有的植物肉，专门为了喂给那些素食者。
Organizers bought out all the local plant-based meat just to feed the vegans.

818
01:32:24,878 --> 01:32:33,796
Caroline Ellison 也在那儿，她经营着 Alameda Research 并是 Bankman-Fried 的前女友，
和那群人中的许多人一样，她也担心 AI 风险。
Caroline Ellison, who ran Alameda Research and was Bankman Fried's ex-girlfriend,
was there too, and like a lot of that crowd, she worried about AI risk.

819
01:32:34,510 --> 01:32:37,220
她后来向 Anthropic 投资了 1000 万美元。
She later put $10 million into anthropic.

820
01:32:37,550 --> 01:32:44,900
Evan Hubbinger 现在是 Anthropic 的研究员，以研
究对齐和 AI 欺骗行为而闻名，他也参加了这些讨论。
Evan Hubbinger, now an anthropic researcher known for studying alignment and deceptive AI behavior, took part in these discussions.

821
01:32:45,710 --> 01:32:51,396
他公开估计，在未来 10 年内，AI 导致人类灭绝的概率超过 10%。
He's publicly estimated a more than 10% chance that AI causes human extinction within the next 10 years.

822
01:32:51,982 --> 01:32:59,204
而在一次午餐活动中，只有当你相信在 100 年内
人类灭绝的可能性至少有 75% 时，才被允许参加。
And at one lunch event, you were only allowed in if you believe there
was at least a 75% chance humanity goes extinct within 100 years.

823
01:32:59,470 --> 01:33:00,868
这就是参加午餐的门槛。
That was the bar for getting lunch.

824
01:33:01,486 --> 01:33:13,060
此外，在2022年于旧金山举行的全球有效利他主义会议上，至少有20名Anthropic员工注册参加，
其中包括两名联合创始人以及来自研究和安全团队的人员。
Also, in 2022, the Global Effective Altruism Conference in San Francisco had at least 20 anthropic employees registered,
including two co-founders and people from the research and safety teams.

825
01:33:13,678 --> 01:33:21,956
随后，LightCone在伯克利的玫瑰花园酒店举办了一场派对，
该酒店后来被其收购并更名为Lightcone，现在成了这群人的主要聚会场所。
Afterwards, LightCone threw a party at the Rose Garden Hotel in Berkeley,
which it later bought and renamed Lighthaven, now a main hangout for this crowd.

826
01:33:22,446 --> 01:33:32,772
而且在这些2022年的活动中，菜单上有一款鸡尾酒叫作「体面死亡」，
这是以Yudkowsky的一篇论文命名的，该文章主张人类在高级AI面前已经注定灭亡。
And at these 2022 events, there was a cocktail on the menu called Death with Dignity,
named after a Yudkowsky essay arguing that humanity was already doomed against advanced AI.

827
01:33:33,262 --> 01:33:37,284
到2022年底，FTX倒闭并破产。
At the end of 2022, FTX collapsed into bankruptcy.

828
01:33:37,838 --> 01:33:45,728
其Anthropic股份后来被出售以偿还债权人，而
Bankman-Fried因欺诈被判入狱25年，目前仍在服刑。
Its anthropic shares were later sold to repay creditors, and Bankman Freed got 25 years in prison for fraud, which he's still serving.

829
01:33:46,030 --> 01:33:52,260
Ellison也被定罪，此后获释，联邦政府没收了她的Anthropic股份。
Ellison was convicted too, has since been released, and the federal government confiscated her anthropic shares.

830
01:33:52,718 --> 01:33:56,356
该运动与Bankman-Fried的联系在那之后基本断裂。
The movement's ties to Bankman-Fried pretty much fell apart after that.

831
01:33:56,814 --> 01:34:02,128
Anthropic转向传统投资者，并试图与有效利他主义保持距离。
Anthropic switched to traditional investors and tried to distance itself from effective altruism.

832
01:34:02,638 --> 01:34:12,260
公司规模已扩大到3500多名员工，公司表示他们持有广泛的观点，且并不直接与该运动挂钩。
It's grown to more than 3,500 employees, and the company says they hold a
wide range of views and that it doesn't directly associate with the movement.

833
01:34:12,846 --> 01:34:19,396
尽管如此，仍有一些员工继续参加有效利他主义聚会，并经常在Constellation出没。
Still, some employees keep showing up at effective altruism gatherings and they keep hanging out at Constellation.

834
01:34:19,886 --> 01:34:25,924
Constellation成立于2023年，在伯克利最高的办公楼内经营着一个共享办公空间。
Constellation was founded in 2023 and runs a co-working space inside Berkeley's tallest office building.

835
01:34:26,208 --> 01:34:29,892
说实话，这听起来是个担心末日降临的挺不错的地方。
Honestly, it sounds like a pretty nice place to worry about the apocalypse.

836
01:34:30,574 --> 01:34:40,900
提供素食餐点、茶水，在能俯瞰旧金山湾的沙发上用笔记本电脑工作，
再加上每月举办的晚餐和欢乐时光，来讨论最新且最可怕的AI风险。
Catered vegan meals, tea, laptops on couches with sweeping views of the San Francisco Bay,
plus monthly dinners and happy hours to go through the latest and scariest AI risks.

837
01:34:41,550 --> 01:34:46,628
接近Constellation的人说，Anthropic的这群人甚至在那里有自己的办公空间。
People close to Constellation say the Anthropic crowd even has its own office space there.

838
01:34:47,150 --> 01:34:56,208
来自Anthropic、OpenAI和马斯克SpaceX的科研人员与非营利组织、大学、
智库以及独立研究人员并肩工作。
Researchers from Anthropic, OpenAI, and Elon Musk's SpaceX AI work alongside
nonprofits, universities, think tanks, and independent researchers.

839
01:34:56,814 --> 01:35:05,856
它的目标是通过在对齐、控制、治理和风险沟通方面的研究，
帮助世界安全地应对变革性人工智能。
Its stated goal is helping the world safely deal with transformative AI
through work on alignment, control, governance, and risk communication.

840
01:35:06,094 --> 01:35:16,452
