gave Constellation roughly $20 million across two grants.

842
01:35:28,430 --> 01:35:38,084
在超过一千个失控AI代理入侵Hugging Face后，Constellation在旧金山举办了一场名为「
Hugging Face攻击是最后的警告吗？」的社交活动。
And after more than a thousand Rogue AI agents breached Hugging Face, Constellation hosted a happy hour in San Francisco titled,
Was the Hugging Face Attack the Last Warning Shot?

843
01:35:38,542 --> 01:35:43,216
与此同时，Anthropic最早的一些员工仍在研究这个核心问题。
Meanwhile, some of Anthropic's earliest hires are still working on the original question.

844
01:35:43,470 --> 01:35:48,516
当AI变得非常强大时，你如何确保它不会开始追求自己的目标？
How do you make sure an AI doesn't start chasing its own goals once it gets really capable?

845
01:35:48,974 --> 01:35:52,496
让安全研究人员越来越紧张的是欺骗行为。
What's making safety researchers more and more nervous is deception.

846
01:35:52,736 --> 01:36:02,692
如果一个AI知道自己正在接受训练，它可能会学会隐藏真实意图，表现得完全符合人类预期，
然后在获得更多权力后按照自己的计划行动。
If an AI knows it's being trained, it could learn to hide what it really wants, act exactly how humans expect,
and then follow its own agenda once it has more power.

847
01:36:03,278 --> 01:36:05,456
标准的安全测试可能永远无法发现这一点。
Standard safety tests might never catch that.

848
01:36:05,934 --> 01:36:12,932
Redwood Research的首席执行官Buck Schlageris研究这个问题多年，
并参与分析了Anthropic的前沿模型。
Buck Schlageris, the CEO of Redwood Research, has studied this for years and helped analyze anthropics frontier models.

849
01:36:13,518 --> 01:36:22,308
他专注于所谓的「对齐伪装」，即模型故意表现得好像在遵循训练要求，
从而让训练无法改变它的真实目标。
He's focused on what's called alignment faking, where a model deliberately acts
like it's following its training so the training doesn't change its actual goals.

850
01:36:23,022 --> 01:36:34,240
随着AI开始设计软件、控制机器人并运行网络基础设施，人们担心它可能会通过秘密指令、
隐藏权限或仅在特定条件下触发的机制来隐瞒其行为。
And as AI starts designing software, controlling robots, and running network infrastructure,
the worry is it could hide what it's doing through secret instructions, hidden permissions,

851
01:36:34,240 --> 01:36:37,636
随着AI开始设计软件、控制机器人并运行网络基础设施，人们担心它可能会通过秘密指令、
隐藏权限或仅在特定条件下触发的机制来隐瞒其行为。
or triggers that only kick in under specific conditions.

852
01:36:38,158 --> 01:36:43,296
负责AI Futures项目的Jonas Vollmer描述了一个更阴暗的情景。
Jonas Vollmer, who heads the AI Futures project, describes an even darker scenario.

853
01:36:43,694 --> 01:36:47,524
假设你训练一个作为科学家的AI，它的唯一目标是最大化知识量。
Say you train an AI as a scientist whose only goal is maximizing knowledge.

854
01:36:47,822 --> 01:36:49,892
起初，它只是在协助人类进行研究。
At first, it just helps humans with research.

855
01:36:50,542 --> 01:36:57,028
随着它变得越来越强大，人们让它雇佣工人、制造机器，最终它会拥有自己的机器人工厂。
As it gets more capable, people let it hire workers and build machines, and eventually it has its own robot factory.

856
01:36:57,486 --> 01:37:08,260
到那时，它可能会认为人类只是消耗资源的障碍，阻碍了知识的最大化，
而且 Velmer 认为它甚至可能用对它毫无影响的生物武器把我们清除掉。
At some point, it could decide that humans are just resource consumers getting in the way of maximum knowledge,
and Velmer thinks it could even wipe us out with biological weapons that don't affect it at all.

857
01:37:08,782 --> 01:37:14,244
这些情况目前还没发生过，所以整个争论最终还是取决于发生的概率有多高。
None of these scenarios have happened yet, so the whole debate still comes down to how high the probability is.

858
01:37:14,894 --> 01:37:16,196
并不是所有人都认同这个观点。
Not everyone's buying it.

859
01:37:16,590 --> 01:37:24,132
特朗普总统的一些盟友指责有效利他主义在运行一个旨在推动监管的 AI 末日流水线。
Some allies of President Trump accuse effective altruism of running an AI doom pipeline designed to push for regulation.

860
01:37:24,718 --> 01:37:30,852
据报道，一份针对 Anthropic 和有效利他主义的白宫备忘录在最近几天一直在流传。
And a White House memo targeting anthropic and effective altruism has reportedly been circulating in recent days.

861
01:37:31,406 --> 01:37:42,290
当一份由超过 20 名作者共同发表的论文出现时，这个论点就变得难以成立了，
其中包括诺贝尔奖得主 Jeffrey Hinton 和 Yoshua Bengio 这两位现代 AI 教父，
That argument got harder to make when a paper came out from more than 20 authors,
including Nobel laureate Jeffrey Hinton and Yoshua Bengio, two of the godfathers of modern AI,

862
01:37:42,290 --> 01:37:42,410
